//www.schemecolor.com/","name":"SchemeColor","categoryId":"design-playgrounds","ranking":15,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Browse thousands of beautiful color combinations. It’s like window shopping for your next big project’s aesthetic.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-email-tycoon","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/email-tycoon/","name":"Email Tycoon","categoryId":"look-productive","ranking":17,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Transform the soul-crushing dread of an unread inbox into a thriving corporate empire. It\'s the only time you\'ll actually want to see \'New Message.\'","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"lookingbusy-com","url":"https://www.lookingbusy.com/","name":"LookingBusy","categoryId":"look-productive","ranking":20,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The ultimate camouflage for the corporate slacker. Transform your screen into a flurry of fake activity so you can daydream in total \'busy\' peace.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"beverageindex-com","url":"https://beverageindex.com/","name":"Beverage Index","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":22,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A global leaderboard of drink prices. Find out where your happy hour budget goes the furthest and where a single pint might require a small bank loan.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"zenpencils-com","url":"https://www.zenpencils.com/","name":"Zen Pencils","categoryId":"web-comics","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Famous inspirational quotes transformed into beautiful, bite-sized comic strips. It\'s the therapy session you actually want to attend.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"quoteinvestigator-com","url":"https://quoteinvestigator.com/","name":"Quote Investigator","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":14,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Stop sharing fake Mark Twain quotes. Find out who actually said what in this deep-dive database of verbal receipts.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"tjukanovt-github-io-notable-people","url":"https://tjukanovt.github.io/notable-people","name":"Notable People Map","categoryId":"geo-explore","ranking":16,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A map where the landmarks are people. See which legendary figures were born in your hometown or find out who owns the \'fame\' title in the most remote corners of the world.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"celebheights-com","url":"https://www.celebheights.com/","name":"Celebheights","categoryId":"celebrity-gossip","ranking":1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An obsessive community dedicated to measuring the exact height of every famous person. It’s taller (or shorter) than you think.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"knowyourmeme-com-categories-person","url":"https://knowyourmeme.com/categories/person","name":"Know Your Meme (Celebs)","categoryId":"internet-culture","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Trace the digital DNA of famous people who became internet legends. The encyclopedia of why people are famous.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"famousbirthdays-com","url":"https://www.famousbirthdays.com/","name":"Famous Birthdays","categoryId":"celebrity-gossip","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The Wikipedia of the influencer age. Find out who’s trending and which TikTokers share your birthday.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"adultswim-com-etcetera-elastic-man","url":"https://www.adultswim.com/etcetera/elastic-man/","name":"Elastic Man","categoryId":"odd-satisfy","ranking":36,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Stretch, pull, and release a weirdly elastic face. Satisfying, slightly creepy, and 100% pointless.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"mandalagaba-com","url":"https://www.mandalagaba.com/","name":"Mandalagaba","categoryId":"blank-canvas","ranking":19,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Create complex, hypnotic mandalas with a single stroke. You\'ll feel like a master artist even if you usually struggle to draw a straight line.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nMandalaGaba is a symmetry drawing board that runs in the browser and, if you want, with other people. The canvas opens in a random color with faint axes through the middle, and every line you draw is repeated around the center, so a wobble becomes a petal and a scribble becomes a mandala. Each session has its own address you can send to a friend, who then draws on the same canvas as you, live.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick, hold and drag. Use the panel to set how many symmetry axes you want, whether strokes are mirrored as well as rotated, and pick a color from the wheel, a brush thickness, a line tool or a fill. Undo is one click. Press save to keep the picture, or start a new session for a clean board. To draw together, share the address in the bar or use the button that finds you a drawing partner, and use the little chat box to argue about who ruined it.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nMost symmetry pads are solo toys. This one is a shared room. The forking option lets you take a copy of someone\'s drawing and carry on alone, there is a statistics button, and the whole thing is free of ads and trackers, which is rare for a tool this capable. It is also more of a proper drawing app than a gag, with a real color wheel and a fill tool.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nMost symmetry pads are a solo pastime, and this one hands a second person a brush on the same canvas, live, through a shared address. That makes it the pick for a quiet call with someone far away, or for anyone who wants their doodles to look intentional, since the axes turn a wobble into a petal. The real color wheel and fill tool mean the result can be more than a gag.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with eight or twelve axes, that is where mandalas happen\\n- Use the line tool for clean spokes and the brush for the soft parts\\n- Send the session address to someone and draw at the same time\\n- Fork a session if you want to keep their start and lose their finish\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs MandalaGaba free?\\nYes. It is free in the browser with no ads and no cookie banner. An account is optional.\\n\\nDoes MandalaGaba work on a phone?\\nIt loads in a mobile browser, but drawing is easier on a tablet or a computer.\\n\\nDo I need an account for MandalaGaba?\\nNo. You can draw without one. An account is optional and lets you save to a profile.\\n\\nCan I draw with someone else on MandalaGaba?\\nYes. Every session has a shareable address, and two people can draw on the same canvas at the same time.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bouncyballs-org","url":"https://bouncyballs.org/","name":"Bouncy Balls","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":45,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Make a bunch of colorful balls freak out using your mouse or your microphone. It’s a physics playground that doubles as a noise-o-meter for your desk.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBouncy Balls is a screen full of shiny colored balls that bounce to the noise in the room. It listens through your microphone: a quiet room and the balls settle on the floor, a loud one and they leap up the screen. It was built as a classroom noise meter for teachers, which is why it is polite and ad-free, but on Bored it is a toy you can play with your voice.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress the start button and allow the microphone when the browser asks. Then talk, clap, hum or put music on and watch the balls react, jumping higher the louder the room gets and settling again when it goes quiet. The settings let you swap the balls for emoji, numbers, bubbles or a set of eyeballs, and there is an optional alert that beeps or shushes when the room gets too loud. Your settings are remembered in the browser for next time.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nSound-reactive toys usually want a file or a track. This one wants you, live, and the balls answer every sound the room makes. The eyeballs mode is the one to show people, and the shush alert is a small comedy in itself when it goes off during a serious sentence.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nBouncy Balls moves to your voice rather than your cursor, which most browser toys do not. Clap, hum or put a song on and the balls answer every sound the room makes. A minute with the eyeballs mode is enough to see the joke. It also happens to be a useful gadget if you have a noisy room to manage, which is a bonus Bored rarely offers.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Allow the microphone when asked, nothing happens without it\\n- Try eyeballs mode with a group and watch them start whispering\\n- Set the alert to shush and forget it is on\\n- Put a song on and use it as a very cheap visualizer\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Bouncy Balls free?\\nYes. It is free in the browser with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes Bouncy Balls work on a phone?\\nYes. It runs in a mobile browser and uses the phone\'s microphone once you allow it.\\n\\nDoes Bouncy Balls need the microphone?\\nYes. The balls react to sound from your microphone, and the site does nothing until you allow it.\\n\\nDoes Bouncy Balls save my settings?\\nYes. Your ball style and alert choice are stored in your browser between visits.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"murdle-com","url":"https://murdle.com/","name":"Murdle","categoryId":"mystery-solve","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Channel your inner Poirot with daily logic-based murder mysteries. Use the clues to find the killer, the weapon, and the motive before you become the next victim of boredom.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-who-said-what","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/who-said-what/","name":"Who Said What?","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":26,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Put your literacy to the test and find out if that quote came from a world leader or a cartoon villain. Spoiler: It\'s harder than you think.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade","categoryId":"arcade-portals","name":"Bored.com Arcade","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The motherlode of procrastination. A massive vault of browser games where productivity goes to die and your high scores live forever.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBored.com Arcade is our own collection of browser games, all built in-house and all playable right here: word and vocab puzzles, logic and grid puzzles, trivia and guessing games, action and platformers, 2-player duels, party games and sandboxes. At the time of writing there are 165 games on the page, and a good share of them are dailies with a fresh puzzle every day.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick a game and go. The index sorts by category, newest, most popular or A to Z, and the filter panel narrows by keyword, category or feature: daily, 2-player, no timer. Every game page has a How to play panel, a row of related games and a feedback prompt at the bottom. Nothing needs an account. Best scores and daily results are kept in your browser, so you always have a number to beat.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nNo downloads, no accounts, no ads, no cookie banner, nothing to close before you play. That is the whole idea. The games are small on purpose: a mini crossword, a color-flood grid, a twenty-questions guessing game, a one-minute detective, a fake work screen for when the boss walks past. Most are made to be finished in a break, and the dailies give you a reason to come back tomorrow rather than a reason to stay all night.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nOurs is the small collection, and it is where we send you first, because it is the one we can vouch for game by game. Everything on it was built in-house, most of it to be finished in a break, and the dailies are the reason to come back tomorrow rather than stay all night. Do the daily round, which takes about a coffee, and then the bigger hubs go deeper.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Filter on Daily and do the round, it takes about a coffee\\n- Sort by newest to see what arrived most recently\\n- The No timer filter is the calm list\\n- Your best scores live in this browser, so use the same one\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Bored.com Arcade free?\\nYes. Every game is free, with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes Bored.com Arcade work on a phone?\\nYes. The games are built for touch as well as keyboard, and the index works on any screen.\\n\\nDoes Bored.com Arcade save anything?\\nBest scores and daily results are stored in your browser. There is no account, so they stay on the device you played on.\\n\\nHow often does Bored.com Arcade get new games?\\nNew games arrive regularly and carry a NEW badge for a while, and the dailies refresh every day.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"openfront-io","url":"https://openfront.io/","name":"Openfront.io","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":18,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A high-speed, low-poly tactical shooter that runs in your browser. Perfect for when your meeting is running ten minutes too long.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"frontwars-io","url":"https://frontwars.io","name":"Front Wars","categoryId":"strategy-games","ranking":16,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Turn-based tactical warfare for the armchair general who doesn\'t have time for a full-scale installation.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"rocketgoal-io","url":"https://rocketgoal.io/","name":"RocketGoal.io","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Rocket League’s 2D browser cousin. Boost, flip, and score goals before the physics engine decides you’ve had too much fun.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"redcoats-io-app","url":"https://redcoats.io/app/","name":"Redcoats.io","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":23,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Fight Revolutionary War line-battles in your browser. Stand in a row, wait for the command, and try to remain pixelated.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bloxd-io","url":"https://bloxd.io/","name":"Bloxd.io","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":8,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Minecraft’s leaner, meaner brother that lives in your browser. Build, parkour, and explore without ever touching an install button.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBloxd.io is a browser hub of block-world games: a front page of modes with live player counts, from Bedwars and Skywars team fights to Sandbox Creative, Sandbox Survival, Sandbox Peaceful, One Block, a parkour collection called Parkour Place, and thousands of players in custom games made by other players. The front page counter stood at about 23,000 people playing.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick a mode from the Top Games grid and you are in with a random guest name. It is a keyboard-and-mouse game with the usual block-game controls. Parkour Place bundles more than twenty short courses, the sandbox modes are open worlds, and the team fights are what they sound like. Friends and Party panels let you join a friend\'s server by code. An optional login keeps your progress, and there is a shop and a paid tier if you want extras, neither of which you need.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nChoice without setup. This one is a menu of more than twenty, plus the custom games, and the counts next to each tell you where the people are. There is no download and no account needed for any of it, and guest play really does work.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nIt is the block game you can open in a tab with no install, and we list it for Parkour Place and the sandbox modes. The name does the rest. Know that many modes are PvP with strangers, and that the site itself tells under-13s to ask an adult before playing.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with Parkour Place, it teaches the movement before anyone is fighting you\\n- Sandbox Peaceful is the calm one\\n- Create a party by code if you would rather share a server with friends than strangers\\n- Expect a cookie popup on the first visit, the site runs ads\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Bloxd.io free?\\nYes. It is free to play in the browser. It is ad supported, with a cookie popup on the way in, and the account is optional.\\n\\nDoes Bloxd.io work on a phone?\\nIt is a keyboard-and-mouse game, so a laptop or desktop is the place to play it.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Bloxd.io?\\nNo. You play as a guest under a random name. Logging in is optional and keeps your progress.\\n\\nDoes Bloxd.io save anything?\\nAs a guest, not much. With an account, your progress is kept.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-26","desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"smashkarts-io","url":"https://smashkarts.io/","name":"Smash Karts","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":16,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"3D kart racing where the trophy is optional and blowing up everyone else on the track is the point. Drive fast, grab power-ups, and ruin some friendships.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"50s-myretrotvs-com","url":"https://50s.myretrotvs.com/","name":"My 50s TV","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Journey back to the golden age of black-and-white static, classic sitcoms, and a time when a \'remote\' was just the youngest child in the room.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"60s-myretrotvs-com","url":"https://60s.myretrotvs.com/","name":"My 60s TV","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Tune into the decade of moon landings and psychedelic vibes. It\'s like finding a vintage television in your attic that actually works.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"70s-myretrotvs-com","url":"https://70s.myretrotvs.com/","name":"My 70s TV","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Groovy channel surfing through the era of bell-bottoms and disco. Finally, a way to experience the 70s without the leaded gasoline smell.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"90s-myretrotvs-com","url":"https://90s.myretrotvs.com/","name":"My 90s TV","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":35,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Channel surf through the decade of denim, dial-up, and some very questionable Saturday morning cartoons.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"00s-myretrotvs-com","url":"https://00s.myretrotvs.com/","name":"My 00s TV","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":32,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Relive the Y2K panic and the dawn of reality TV. It\'s a time machine back to when your biggest worry was your MySpace Top 8.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"autosam-github-io-tamaweb","url":"https://autosam.github.io/Tamaweb/","name":"Tamaweb","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":14,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A digital pet that lives in your browser tab. Keep it fed, happy, and alive while you pretend to be working on that spreadsheet.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"rooms-xyz-play","url":"https://rooms.xyz/play","name":"Rooms.xyz","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":23,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A voxel-based playground where you can build, play, and lose your afternoon in someone else\'s 3D fever dream.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"aidn-jp-contents","url":"https://aidn.jp/contents/","name":"AIDN","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A grab bag of Japanese web experiments. Make music with a tap or watch shapes dance. Productivity doesn\'t stand a chance.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nAIDN is the contents page of a Japanese musician and web-toy maker: three grids of animated tiles, sixty-odd browser toys under WEB, a row of music videos under MV, and a handful of odds and ends under OTHERS. The toys are small, loud and strange: a talking tofu, a sword-drawing game, an endless swipe, a wow button with a global counter, gif makers, a cat-run game, a fortune draw, a toy that measures the angle of a twin-tail hairstyle.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nScroll the grid and click a tile. Each toy opens on its own page, many with a click-to-play screen and a request to turn the sound on. Most explain themselves in a second or two, and some have a help button. Come back to the grid for the next one. Titles are a mix of Japanese and English, and the tiles are looping previews, so you can tell what a thing is before you open it.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nEverything here is made by one maker with one sensibility, and the sound is the point: the toys are built around loops, taps and beats, and several are music videos you can play with. A famous virtual singer character stars in a lot of them, along with the maker\'s own cat and green-haired mascots. It is the kind of collection where the fifth tile is as good as the first and there are sixty.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nA whole shelf of loud, pointless toys from a corner of the web most people never reach. Sound on, headphones ideally. There is nothing to read, so the language does not matter.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Sound on before you click anything, it is the whole point\\n- The wow button is the quickest way to understand the site\\n- The MV row is music videos, some interactive, save them for when you have five minutes\\n- Tiles loop, so watch before you click\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs AIDN free?\\nYes. Everything on it is free in the browser with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes AIDN work on a phone?\\nYes. Most of the toys are tap toys and work well with touch.\\n\\nDoes AIDN have sound?\\nYes, and many toys ask you to turn it on before they start. It is a music maker\'s site.\\n\\nHow many toys does AIDN have?\\nSixty-odd under WEB at the time of writing, plus the music videos and extras.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-28","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"technooptimism-org-archive","url":"https://technooptimism.org/archive/","name":"Techno-Optimism Archive","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A digital excavation of the future we were promised. Dive into the archives of tech optimism to see the inventions that almost changed the world.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikihow-com-which-the-boys-character-am-i","url":"https://www.wikihow.com/Which-the-Boys-Character-Am-I","name":"Which The Boys Character Am I?","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Find out if your soul is anxious, calculating, or completely unhinged with a personality questionnaire built to match you with your The Boys counterpart.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"crazygames-com","url":"https://www.crazygames.com/","name":"CrazyGames","categoryId":"arcade-portals","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A massive sandbox of over 4,500 free browser games across every genre imaginable. No installs, no updates, just pure unadulterated procrastination.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nCrazyGames is one of the big browser-game portals, a dark-theme grid of thousands of games with a mood row at the top: train your brain, adrenaline rush, with friends, 5-minute fun, meme and bloxy, timeless classics, just relax, deep progress. Under that come top games in your country today, featured, new, the site\'s own originals, timed leaderboards and a category strip from driving and trivia to word, .io and board games.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick a tile. Game pages list a rating, the release date, the engine, the platforms the game runs on, a long description with controls and a FAQ. Guest play works. An optional account and a paid tier with perks are there if you want them, and the homepage runs timed leaderboards with hundreds of thousands of players ranked. The site detects a controller if you have one plugged in and offers the games that support it. Expect a cookie popup on the first visit and ads around the frame.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe moods and the metadata. Most portals sort by genre. This one also sorts by how much time and energy you have, and the 5-minute fun row is exactly what it says. The game pages tell you the engine, whether a game is an emulated classic, and which devices it supports, which saves you a click. The top games list is per country, so it changes depending on where you are.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThe signposting is the reason. Close to twenty of our links point at individual games here, including emulated originals from the plugin era, and the mood row at the top is the quickest way we know to match a game to the size of your break. Five-minute fun means five minutes and deep progress means a weekend. A visit is as long as you tell it to be.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with 5-minute fun on a break and deep progress on a weekend\\n- Read the platforms line on a game page before playing on a phone\\n- Timeless classics is the row for older games\\n- Plug in a controller, the site will tell you which games use it\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs CrazyGames free?\\nYes. The games are free with no account required. The site is ad supported, with a cookie popup on the first visit and an optional paid tier.\\n\\nDoes CrazyGames work on a phone?\\nYes. The site works on any screen, and each game page lists whether the game supports desktop, mobile or tablet.\\n\\nDo I need an account for CrazyGames?\\nNo. Guest play works. An account is optional.\\n\\nHow many games does CrazyGames have?\\nThousands. The homepage alone links to nearly three hundred, and new games are added daily.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"poki-com","url":"https://poki.com/","name":"Poki","categoryId":"arcade-portals","ranking":8,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A giant playground of free online browser games. Tap in instantly to play hundreds of high-quality casual games solo or with friends.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nPoki is one of the biggest browser-game portals in the world, run by a team in Amsterdam since 2014. The homepage is a wall of tiles, about 1,500 games by the site\'s own count, sorted into nearly forty categories from car and puzzle games to dress-up, .io, cozy, stickman and typing games. Every game plays in a tab on desktop, phone or tablet, and the site says it tests each one itself.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick a tile. Each game page has the game up top, a like and dislike count, a fullscreen button, and a long page of text underneath with the controls, the mechanics and a FAQ. A short video ad runs before most games. Guest play works without an account, and an optional account saves progress across devices. There is a top-five trending list on the homepage based on what is being played right now.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nCuration at scale. The counts are large, over a hundred million players a month, over a hundred and fifty multiplayer games, over two hundred and fifty puzzles, but the site reads like it is picked rather than dumped, with licensed games sitting next to the site\'s own exclusives. The game pages are unusually complete: you can learn a game from the text before you play it. And the site runs in what it calls family-friendly mode, with contextual, non-personalized ads and no cookie popup.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nAbout thirty of our game links point at pages here, so if one of them hooked you, this is where it lives and where its neighbors are. The hub itself is the polished one among the giants: a wall of tiles that reads as picked rather than dumped, with a page of controls and mechanics under every game so you can learn it before you play. The trending five gives a browse a place to start.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with the trending five, it is live data\\n- Read the page under the game for controls before you rage-quit\\n- Make an account only if you play the same game on two devices\\n- The 2 Player category is the one for a shared keyboard\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Poki free?\\nYes. Every game is free with no account required. The site is ad supported, with a video ad before most games.\\n\\nDoes Poki work on a phone?\\nYes. The site says all games are playable on mobile, tablet and desktop, and each game page lists its supported devices.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Poki?\\nNo. Guest play works. An optional account keeps your progress across devices.\\n\\nHow many games does Poki have?\\nAbout 1,500 by the site\'s own count, with new releases added daily.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-owls","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/owls/","name":"Owls","categoryId":"brain-train","ranking":27,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Sudoku, but make it nocturnal. Deduce where to place one owl per row and column before your brain completely shorts out.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-hero-of-mediocria","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/hero-of-mediocria/","name":"Hero of Mediocria","categoryId":"adventure-games","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Armed with a stolen Wi-Fi router and a sword, whack monsters to save your favorite show in this wonderfully addictive browser RPG.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"loadingartist-com","url":"https://loadingartist.com/","name":"Loading Artist","categoryId":"web-comics","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Witty and beautifully illustrated webcomics exploring modern anxiety, work culture, and creative struggles. Don\'t forget to look for the hidden spider.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"isabisabel-com-gacha","url":"https://isabisabel.com/gacha/","name":"Number Gacha","categoryId":"idle-clicker-games","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A gacha game where you roll, unpack, and battle numbers. Pure gacha, distilled to its essence.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nNumber Gacha is a gacha game where the prizes are numbers. One hundred of them, hidden behind a grid of question marks. You roll, a number drops out with a rarity banner and a little quote attached, and the grid fills in one slot at a time. It sounds like nothing. It will be open in a tab for a week.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nHit Roll. Each roll costs one diamond, you start with ten, and they refill on a timer, so the game paces itself. Every number arrives as a card with a rarity tier and something to say about itself. Duplicates happen, that is the gacha part. Keep rolling until the grid has no question marks left. The info button in the corner has a reset if you ever want to start over, and as the collection grows, other currencies and things to do with your numbers start to appear.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe whole loot box economy, the timers, the rarity tiers, the tiny ping when a rare one drops, applied to the most worthless collectible imaginable. There is no shop and nothing to buy, so it works as a small joke about gacha games while also being a weirdly good one. Every number has its own flavor text, so pulling 39 feels less like a roll and more like meeting a character.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nIt is the rare idle game that is in on the joke. No microtransactions, no energy to buy, just the pull of a rarity banner and a grid slowly filling in. The perfect tab to keep open behind whatever you are supposed to be doing.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Leave the tab open, the diamonds refill whether you watch or not\\n- Check back a few times a day instead of burning all ten at once\\n- Read the quotes, some numbers have opinions\\n- When in doubt, keep rolling. That is the game\'s own advice and it is correct\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Number Gacha free?\\nYes. Free in the browser, no account, no ads, and there is nothing to buy, which is the joke.\\n\\nDoes Number Gacha save my collection?\\nYes, your progress is stored in the browser, so keep using the same device and browser to carry on.\\n\\nHow long does it take to collect all 100 numbers in Number Gacha?\\nDays, not minutes. Diamonds refill on a timer and duplicates slow down the last stretch, exactly like a real gacha.\\n\\nDoes Number Gacha work on a phone?\\nYes. It runs in a mobile browser as well as on a desktop.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-10","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikihow-com-euphoria-character-quiz","url":"https://www.wikihow.com/Euphoria-Character-Quiz","name":"Which Euphoria Character Am I?","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Walk through a quick set of lifestyle questions to discover which character from the hit show Euphoria matches your inner chaos.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikihow-com-who-is-your-euphoria-soulmate-quiz","url":"https://www.wikihow.com/Who-Is-Your-Euphoria-Soulmate-Quiz","name":"Who Is Your Euphoria Soulmate Quiz","categoryId":"love-games","ranking":-1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Take this short interactive questionnaire to reveal which Euphoria companion is officially destined to be your soulmate.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikihow-com-what-pokemon-are-you","url":"https://www.wikihow.com/What-Pokemon-Are-You","name":"What Pokémon Are You","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":18,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Answer honestly about your daily habits and discover which classic pocket monster represents your true spiritual identity.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"techyonic-co-swiftle","url":"https://www.techyonic.co/swiftle","name":"Swiftle","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Name that Taylor Swift track in under a second. Put your pop-culture music trivia through a timeline stress test.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"addictinggames-com","url":"https://www.addictinggames.com","name":"Addicting Games","categoryId":"arcade-portals","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The grandfather of online game portals is still alive and kicking. Relive your school computer lab glory days with thousands of updated, instantly playable titles.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nAddicting Games is the old-school portal, still running and still red and black: over five thousand free browser games by its own count, sorted into categories from action, car, card and clicker to .io, puzzle, shooting, snake, sports, strategy and zombie, with tags for everything from avoider to tower defense. It is updated every Thursday, the meta description says, and the homepage has a Most Addicting row of the classics that built the site.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nScroll the rows, new games, most addicting, indie spotlight, trending, top 100, or pick a category from the left rail. Click a tile and the game opens in the page. Guest play works and favorites are kept in your browser. A profile is optional. The site also runs an Indie Spotlight of playable demos ahead of their store releases, a daily games list with word, sudoku, kakuro and sokoban puzzles, and a gaming news column.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe canon. The Most Addicting row is the plugin-era hall of fame, the block-rolling puzzle, the helicopter game, the tug-of-war strategy, the unfair quiz, all still playable. Next to that, the indie demos are new and the daily puzzles are a habit. The site promises no intrusive ads or pop-ups, while showing a cookie popup and ad slots, which is the kind of promise a portal makes.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThis is the hub your older sibling used, and the Most Addicting row is why: the block-rolling puzzle, the helicopter game, the unfair quiz, all still playable. Come for that row first and the daily puzzles second. The dailies are a quiet corner that earns a bookmark. The classics are a short visit each and the dailies are a habit. There is a Parents and Guardians page in the footer if you need one.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Most addicting is the nostalgia row, start there\\n- Daily games is a quiet corner worth a bookmark\\n- Indie spotlight has real demos, not trailers\\n- Top 100 is the quick way into the back catalog\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Addicting Games free?\\nYes. The games are free with no account required. The site is ad supported, with a cookie popup on the first visit.\\n\\nDoes Addicting Games work on a phone?\\nYes. The site says its games play on desktop or mobile.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Addicting Games?\\nNo. Guest play works and favorites are kept in your browser. A profile is optional.\\n\\nHow many games does Addicting Games have?\\nOver five thousand by the site\'s own count, updated weekly.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"pogo-com","url":"https://www.pogo.com/","name":"Pogo","categoryId":"arcade-portals","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"EA\'s classic home for puzzle, card, and board game enthusiasts. Kick back with smooth, browser-based casual titles that require zero setup but deliver endless distraction.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nPogo is the casual-games site of a big games publisher: sixty-odd browser games in the classic casual genres, solitaire, word, mahjong, puzzle, match 3, board, card, hidden object and multiplayer, with a daily challenge in several of them and a playing-now count on the top games. The games are few, finished and tidy.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nBrowse all games or use the jump-to chips, one per genre plus top, new and best mobile. Click Play and the game opens in the page. Guest play works without an account. Registering, free, saves your progress across devices, adds challenges and badges, and removes ads for two days. Club Pogo is the paid tier. Cookie preferences sit in the footer rather than in a wall.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe audience. This is the portal for people who want one good game of solitaire or a word game with a mascot, played every day for years, not a wall of three thousand tiles. The games are licensed and finished rather than uploaded, the daily challenges give the regulars a reason to log in, and the badge system keeps them collecting. Sixty-odd games and a row of chips, which after the twenty-thousand-tile portals feels like a day off.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nSixty-odd games instead of a wall of thousands, and every one of them finished. This is the small, tidy hub for the card-and-word crowd, the people who want one good game of solitaire every day for years, and it is where to send someone who found the bigger sites exhausting. Register or do not, the games play either way.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Try the six-letter word game first, it has a playing-now count for a reason\\n- Do the daily challenge, the badges pile up on their own\\n- Guest play is fine for a visit, register only when you want progress kept\\n- Best mobile games is the row to check on a phone\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Pogo free?\\nYes. The games are free to play as a guest. Registration is free and removes ads for two days, and Club Pogo is the paid tier.\\n\\nDoes Pogo work on a phone?\\nYes. The site has a Best mobile games row for exactly that.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Pogo?\\nNo. Guest play works. A free account saves progress across devices and adds challenges and badges.\\n\\nDoes Pogo save anything?\\nAs a guest, only in your browser. With a free account, progress follows you across devices.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-battle-stair","categoryId":"rpg-games","name":"Battle Stair","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/battle-stair/","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Lead a 4-hero party up a treacherous, biome-shifting tower to take down the Voidlord. A surprisingly tactical turn-based RPG that packs a full campaign\'s worth of loot, shops, and strategic combat right into your browser tab.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-word-groups","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/word-groups/","name":"Word Groups","categoryId":"word-nerd","ranking":34,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Group words by their secret connections. It\'s like unraveling a corporate conspiracy, but with vocabulary.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-spelling-bee","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/honey-words/","name":"Honey Words","categoryId":"word-nerd","ranking":32,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Create as many words as you can from a handful of letters. See if your vocabulary can outsmart a hive of digital bees.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-letter-box","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/letter-box/","name":"Letter Box","categoryId":"word-nerd","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Connect letters to build words around a box. A geometric brain-teaser that will push your language skills to the edge.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-daily-trivia","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/daily-trivia/","name":"Daily Trivia","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":49,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A fresh batch of brain-busting questions every single day. A playground for anyone who hoards useless knowledge.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nDaily trivia is ten multiple-choice questions, once a day. The questions roam across geography, science, history, pop culture, food and drink, language and sport, four options each, with the result shown the moment you pick. Score seven or better and your streak survives another day. Three themed packs, movies and TV, video games and music, each add their own daily round if the general one was not enough.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress start or hit enter. Read the question, pick one of the four answers, see whether you were right, move on. Ten questions later you get your score and, if it was seven or more, your streak goes up by one. Miss the mark and the streak resets, so the seventh right answer is the one that matters. Then try a themed pack, movies and TV, video games or music: those questions come with a short explanation after each answer, so you learn something even when you guess wrong. Share your result with the share button.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nMost daily quizzes are either trivially easy or written for pub-quiz veterans. This one aims at the middle, and the pass mark makes a seven feel like a win rather than a miss. The themed packs are the surprise, because the explanations turn a quiz into a small lesson.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThe daily-puzzle habit deserved a general-knowledge version that does not need a dictionary, so we made one of our own. Ten questions, a few minutes, done until tomorrow, with a pass mark of seven that keeps a streak alive without demanding perfection. The themed packs add a short explanation after each answer, which is where a quick round turns into a small lesson.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Seven is the pass mark, so a streak does not need perfection\\n- Do the general round first, then the packs, each has its own daily set\\n- Read the explanations in the packs, they are where the learning is\\n- Enter starts the quiz on a keyboard, no clicking needed\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Daily trivia free?\\nYes. It is one of our own arcade games, no account and no ads.\\n\\nDoes Daily trivia work on a phone?\\nYes. Tap the answers on a phone, or use the keyboard on a computer.\\n\\nHow often does Daily trivia get new questions?\\nEvery day. The general round and each themed pack get a fresh set daily.\\n\\nDoes Daily trivia save my streak?\\nYes. Your streak is kept in your browser on the device you play on.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-country-guess","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/country-guess/","name":"Country Guess","categoryId":"geo-games","ranking":24,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Look at silhouettes and hints to identify the mystery nation. Prove your geography skills extend past finding your own house on a map.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-mahjong","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/mahjong/","name":"Mahjong","categoryId":"puzzle-games","ranking":25,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The legendary tile-matching strategy game, beautifully streamlined for your browser. Perfect for turning a five-minute break into a therapeutic hour.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-solitaire","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/solitaire/","name":"Solitaire","categoryId":"card-games","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The legendary solo card game that got an entire generation through dull afternoons. Sort those decks and chase that satisfying card-cascade.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-stack","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/stack/","name":"Stack","categoryId":"puzzle-games","ranking":32,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Drop blocks precisely on top of each other to build the tallest tower possible. One misplaced pixel and your architectural masterpiece crumbles.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-higher-lower","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/higher-lower/","name":"Higher Lower","categoryId":"estimation-games","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A high-stakes guessing game where you predict whether the next stat is up or down. Deceptively simple, endlessly addictive.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-match-three","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/jewel-forge/","name":"Jewel Forge","categoryId":"puzzle-games","ranking":33,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Swap and click to align three or more glowing gems. Pure, unadulterated dopamine mechanics that will make your afternoon vanish.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"thede-co-getrich-html","categoryId":"pointless-fun","name":"Get Rich Quick","url":"https://thede.co/getrich.html","ranking":60,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A speculative click that promises to make you infinitely wealthy, or at least waste a few seconds of your afternoon.","dateAdded":"2026-01-01","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nGet Rich Quick is a thirty-second trading game in an amber-on-black terminal, scanlines included. A single made-up stock jitters along a line chart in real time before you have pressed anything, with its price and change in a ticker line and a clock. Under the chart, four readouts: POSITION, NET P&L, ALPHA and TIME. One wide button says START SESSION. The page\'s own title says it plainly: get rich in 30 seconds.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress START SESSION, or Enter. The timer counts down from thirty and the button splits into BUY and SHORT, with Q and W as the keyboard shortcuts. Buy opens a long position, and the button becomes SELL. Short opens a short, and the button becomes COVER. You can flip between the two as often as the price tempts you, and the readouts update live: your position\'s running result, your net P&L, and alpha, which is what you made minus what simply holding the stock would have made over the same seconds. At zero the screen says MARKET CLOSE with your final numbers, a box for your name, and an END SESSION button.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe alpha line. The game tells you whether your trades beat doing nothing, which is a harder and more honest question, and the two numbers can disagree. The stock is a random walk, with its volatility and drift shown in the ticker line, so there is nothing to study, only timing and nerve. The leaderboard has a LAST 24H tab and an ALL TIME tab with rank, name, P&L and alpha, and a name is optional: leave it blank and you see the board without being on it.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThirty seconds is exactly long enough to make two decisions and regret one of them. The game knows that and gives you the score, the leaderboard and the NEW SESSION button before the regret has faded, which is the whole loop in under a minute.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Q and W trade, Enter starts and ends, the mouse is optional\\n- The chart runs before you start, so watch a few seconds of it first\\n- Alpha can be positive while P&L is negative, they are two different scores\\n- Leave the name box empty if you only want to look at the leaderboard\\n- Names on the board are typed by players and not filtered, so expect anything\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Get Rich Quick free?\\nYes. No ads, no cookie banner, no account.\\n\\nDoes Get Rich Quick work on a phone?\\nYes. The page is set up for phone screens.\\n\\nDoes Get Rich Quick save my progress?\\nNo. Nothing is kept in the browser. A score goes to the public leaderboard only if you type a name and it qualifies.\\n\\nDoes Get Rich Quick end?\\nYes. Every session is thirty seconds and ends at MARKET CLOSE, with NEW SESSION on the leaderboard screen.\\n\\nDoes Get Rich Quick have sound?\\nNo.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-10-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"make-everything-ok-com","url":"https://make-everything-ok.com/","name":"Make Everything OK","categoryId":"feel-good","ranking":20,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Bad day at the office? This legendary single-button tool is here to help. Click the screen, wait for the processing loop to load comfort metrics, and let the browser fix your digital aura.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"ncase-itch-io-wbwwb","url":"https://ncase.itch.io/wbwwb","name":"We Become What We Behold","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":68,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A brilliant, 5-minute interactive simulation detailing how viral framing and social media feedback loops generate systematic chaos and social anxiety. Point, click, snap photos, and watch the tiny pixel crowd react.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nWe Become What We Behold is a short browser game about how news cycles feed on themselves. You hold a camera over a small crowd of round and square people and decide what to photograph. Whatever you frame becomes the headline, the crowd reacts to the headline, and the next photo is easier to find than the last. The game describes itself as being about news cycles, vicious cycles and infinite cycles, and it earns all three.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nLoad the page and press play on the embedded game. Move the camera over the crowd, watch for anything that looks like a story, and take the shot. The screen at the top shows what your picture turned into. Keep photographing. There is no score and no way to lose, only the crowd changing in response to what you chose to show it. Plan for about five minutes with sound on, since the game uses audio to tell its story.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nPlenty of games are about media. This one puts you behind the lens and lets the mechanic make the argument, with no lecture attached. You will notice things about your own choices before the game says a word about them. The author released all of the code and art into the public domain, and fans have translated it into eleven languages, which is its own small comment on how quickly things spread.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nMost toys here come with no lesson attached. This is the exception we make room for: a five-minute gag that lands a real point and then lets you go. It is the kind of link people send to each other years after they first played it.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Sound on, the game leans on it\\n- Try photographing nothing interesting for a while and see what the crowd does\\n- It is short, so play it through once before reading anything about it\\n- The source code and art are free to remix if you want to build on it\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs We Become What We Behold free?\\nYes. It is free to play in the browser on the maker\'s itch.io page, with no ads and no account needed. The optional support button is a tip jar, not a paywall.\\n\\nIs We Become What We Behold open source?\\nYes. The page says all of the code and art were released to the public domain, with the source linked from the page.\\n\\nDoes We Become What We Behold work on a phone?\\nThe page is built for phones and desktops, but the game itself runs in an embedded window, so a larger screen is the safer bet.\\n\\nCan I play We Become What We Behold in another language?\\nYes. The page links fan translations in eleven languages, including German, French, Polish and Chinese.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-12","desktopOnly":true,"daily":false},{"id":"zty-pe","url":"https://zty.pe/","name":"ZType","categoryId":"typing-speed","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A glorious space arcade shooter where your weapon is your keyboard. Shoot down oncoming enemy word clusters by typing them as fast as humanly possible before you get overwhelmed.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"adultswim-com-etcetera-soup","url":"https://www.adultswim.com/etcetera/soup/","name":"Soup","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Stir a digital vat of graphical chaos in this interactive sensory sandbox. Drag your mouse to swirl abstract geometric patterns and visual noise into a soothing vector soup.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nSoup is a vat of tiny pixel-art characters. The word SOUP sits on a black screen, spelled out in a thick wobbling blob made of hundreds of small cartoon characters, and the only instruction on the start screen is click to start. The page calls it Character Soup. There is no goal and no score, just a mass of figures that flows and settles like thick liquid when you disturb it.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick to start, then click and hold anywhere on the screen. A pixel-art faucet appears under the cursor and pours a fresh cluster of characters into the soup, which spreads out and smears the letters as the mass finds its level. A Zoom slider top left shrinks or enlarges the whole pile. A Drain button top right lets the level sink: the whole mass slides down and out of the letters over several seconds, and a click and hold afterward pours a small new puddle onto the empty floor.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe ingredients are the difference. Liquid toys usually push dots around, this one pushes a crowd. At the default zoom the characters are specks, tiny cartoon figures in many colors tumbling over each other, and the slider changes how big the pile is. The physics is the joke: a crowd that behaves like gravy. Drain is the other half of it, because watching a word made of characters drain out of its letters is a better finish than any score screen.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nA liquid made of tiny characters is a strong entry among the toys you fiddle with for a minute with nothing to win. One click and hold does the trick, the slider and the drain give you two more things to try, and then you leave. It is a toy that rewards a second look.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Hold the click longer than feels polite, the faucet keeps pouring\\n- Pour a second cluster next to the first and watch it flow into the soup\\n- Move the Zoom slider to change the size of the pile\\n- Drain first, then pour, if you want a clean puddle to play with\\n- The cookie dialog has an Essential Cookies Only button inside Manage Preferences\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Soup free?\\nYes. A cookie popup covers the page on arrival, with Accept and Manage Preferences. There are no ads around the toy.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Soup?\\nNo. There is no sign in anywhere on the page.\\n\\nDoes Soup work on a phone?\\nIt should. The page is set up for phone screens and the controls are a press and hold, a slider and a button.\\n\\nDoes Soup end?\\nNo. You pour, you drain, you pour again.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-10-13","desktopOnly":true,"daily":false},{"id":"gradient-horse","url":"https://gradient.horse/","name":"Gradient.horse","categoryId":"crowd-experiments","ranking":23,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Draw a terrible horse on an interactive color canvas, then watch an algorithm animate it to run wild in an endless running loop with horses drawn by other internet strangers.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"madebyevan-com-rapt-play-rapt","url":"https://madebyevan.com/rapt/play/","name":"Rapt","categoryId":"co-op-games","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A slick, vector-styled browser platformer packing complex physics puzzles and razor-sharp collision mechanics. No updates, no loading lags, just pure side-scrolling precision.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"nothingprivate-gkr-pw","url":"https://nothingprivate.gkr.pw/","name":"Are you anonymous?","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":30,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Think incognito mode makes you completely invisible? This striking demonstration reads your unique browser fingerprint to prove websites can track your device even after clearing all your data.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"oldcomputers-net","url":"https://oldcomputers.net/","name":"Steve\'s Old Computer Museum","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":18,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A digital time machine tracking the earliest personal computers known to humanity. Browse obsolete 8-bit machines, read original retail spec sheets, and laugh at what counted as futuristic in 1982.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"candywrapperarchive-com","url":"https://www.candywrapperarchive.com/","name":"Candy Wrapper Archive","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":36,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An obsessive graphic database dedicated entirely to the preservation of vintage candy wrappers. Scroll through sweet nostalgia across generations and trace how your favorite treats used to look on grocery shelves.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"publicdomainreview-org","url":"https://publicdomainreview.org/","name":"The Public Domain Review","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":19,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A handsome online journal digging through history\'s most compelling, bizarre, and beautiful public domain art, literature, and illustrations. Stare at medieval occult charts or centuries-old tactical drawings.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"duckeys-com","url":"https://duckeys.com/","name":"Duckeys","categoryId":"weird-shops","ranking":8,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An online boutique dedicated entirely to mechanical keyboard charms and desktop fidget keys that literally quack, meow, or ribbit when pressed.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"piliapp-com-emoji-download","url":"https://www.piliapp.com/emoji/download/","name":"Emoji Download","categoryId":"emoji-fun","ranking":0,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Copy, paste, and download high-resolution emoji graphics from Apple, Google, Twitter, and more. Perfect for when you need a giant, crisp asset of the thinking face emoji.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"coolinfographics-com","url":"https://coolinfographics.com/","name":"Cool Infographics","categoryId":"data-beautiful","ranking":25,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A glorious visual archive showcasing the most impressive infographics and data visualizations from across the web. Prepare to lose your entire afternoon looking at maps of things you didn\'t know you cared about.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"zapsplat-com","url":"https://www.zapsplat.com/","name":"Zapsplat","categoryId":"audio-toys","ranking":2,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A massive repository of free, professional sound effects and audio tracks. Whether you need the sound of a cartoon frying pan or a haunting ambient spaceship drone, this archive has you covered.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"nga-gov-artworks","url":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks","name":"National Gallery of Art","categoryId":"virtual-museum","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Take a zero-cost cultural tour through thousands of high-definition digital masterpieces. Sift through classical paintings, zoom in to see raw oil paint textures, and browse historic collections from your couch.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"potatoortomato-com","url":"https://potatoortomato.com/","name":"Potato or Tomato","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":50,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A gloriously simple push-your-luck web toy where you look at a vegetable (or fruit) and guess whether it\'s a potato or a tomato. That\'s literally the whole experience.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nPotato or Tomato is a dark page with a chunky white headline, one cartoon drawing in the middle and two red buttons underneath that say POTATO and TOMATO. The drawing zooms in a second after the page loads. Look at it, decide which of the two it is, press the matching button. That is the whole game, and the page has no instructions because it does not need any.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick POTATO or TOMATO. A wrong guess flashes NO NO NO in red across the picture for a second and leaves the same picture there for another try, with no penalty and no score. A right guess brings a cheer in the headline font, a line about how many people have guessed wrong, confetti falling over the whole page, and two links: a share link with a pre-written post, and Play Again, which reloads the page for a fresh drawing. The page picks between its two drawings at random on every load, so the next round may be the same picture again.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nTwo drawings. The page\'s script carries exactly one potato and one tomato, a brown potato and a red tomato with a cut half, and tints the buttons brown or red to match. The joke is in the straight face: a full result screen with confetti and a share button for a question nobody has ever needed to think about, and a wrong-answer path that exists only so the page can shout NO at you.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThere is a pleasure in being asked a question you cannot fail and being congratulated anyway. The confetti takes a second longer than the decision, which is the right ratio for a page you will open once, show someone, and then open again.\\n\\nTips:\\n- The drawing zooms in a moment after the page loads, wait for it\\n- A wrong guess costs nothing, the picture stays and you guess again\\n- Play Again is a page reload, so the next drawing is a new random pick of the same two\\n- The share link has the post written for you, hashtag included\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Potato or Tomato free?\\nYes. No ads, no cookie banner and no account.\\n\\nDoes Potato or Tomato work on a phone?\\nYes. The two buttons are the whole interface.\\n\\nDoes Potato or Tomato end?\\nEach round ends with the right guess. Play Again reloads the page for another.\\n\\nDoes Potato or Tomato have sound?\\nNo.\\n\\nDoes Potato or Tomato save my progress?\\nNo. There is nothing to save, a reload starts a new round.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-10-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"heeeeeeeey-com","url":"https://heeeeeeeey.com/","name":"Heeeeeeeey","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A legendary internet infinite loop that bounces you back and forth between two domains just to chant \\"Hey!\\" and \\"Hoo!\\".","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nHeeeeeeeey is two web pages that throw you between them. The first is white with one word in huge black type, HEEEEEEEEEY with an exclamation mark, sized to fill the window. After one second the page sends you to a second domain, which is the same thing inverted, black with a white HOOOOOOOOO, and after one second that page sends you back. That is the entire site. There is a small maker credit and a share button in the corners and nothing else to click.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nOpen it and leave it. The two words alternate every second for as long as the tab is open. There are no controls, no settings and no end, only the back button or closing the tab when you have had enough.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nIt is a loop between two domains rather than one page animating, so the address bar flips along with the colors. The page source still carries a disabled audio player built to play a hey clip on one page and a ho clip on the other and jump when each finished, so the site was wired to shout and now does not. The current version is silent and runs on a fixed timer, which makes it a metronome of typography rather than a soundboard. The code is from an older web, and it still runs.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nTwo words taking turns is about as little as a website can do, and it does it with total commitment. It is the kind of link you send with no explanation and let the other person work out when to close the tab.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Leave it open in a background tab and glance at it now and then\\n- The words scale to the window, so a big screen gets a big HEY\\n- Closing the tab is the cleanest exit\\n- Nothing to tap, the flipping is automatic\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Heeeeeeeey free?\\nYes. No ads, no cookie banner, no account.\\n\\nDoes Heeeeeeeey work on a phone?\\nYes. The word fits the screen width.\\n\\nDoes Heeeeeeeey have sound?\\nNo. The audio code in the page is switched off, so the chant is visual only.\\n\\nDoes Heeeeeeeey end?\\nNo. It bounces between the two pages until you close the tab.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"playdaily-org","url":"https://playdaily.org/","name":"Play Daily","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":34,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A daily hub offering a fresh collection of quick, addictive puzzle games like Word Hunt and Traffic Jam to challenge your brain every morning.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nPlay Daily is a hub of browser games under one roof, dated at the top like a newspaper. The front page leads with the site\'s own word races, Krillion, Noillirk and Krillocity, all badged multiplayer, where seven prompts come up and you name answers that are rare, or common, or as many as you can, in live rooms the site says hold up to 16 or 30 players for two of them. Below those are music games built on short song clips, a word ladder, an estimation game, a color memory test, a logo color quiz, a globe-tapping geography game, and a Classics row of six quick games, which the tiles describe as a timed letter grid, a free-the-car traffic puzzle, a block-fitting puzzle, a coin maze with a chaser, a key-collecting air hockey table and a 30 day money sim.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick a tile and press Play. The letter grid classic opens a card with a score and a two-minute clock, then a four-by-four grid of letter tiles with a Shuffle button marked x3, and you make words from the tiles before the time runs out. The races run a timer per prompt, 20 to 30 seconds depending on the game, and the site\'s own article on Krillocity says its daily race deals the same seven prompts to everyone, resets at midnight UTC and can be shared without spoiling an answer. The site says its unlimited games have no daily cap.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe three word races are a family: name what nobody else names, name what everybody would say, or name as many as you can while rare answers swim furthest along a seabed. Guide articles under Stories cover the newest one. The catch is the business model: a cookie popup with 315 partners on load, a sticky banner across the bottom of every page including inside a game, and a Daily Pro page that sells the ads away for a yearly or one-time price while the games themselves stay free for everyone.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nMore than a dozen games, several of them daily, with a live multiplayer race on top, is a full morning routine on one bookmark, and the classics row keeps the quick ones a tap away. The ads are the price of admission.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Press Settings on the cookie popup, Reject all is behind it\\n- The letter grid gives you three shuffles, use them when the grid dries up\\n- The daily race resets at midnight UTC, the unlimited games do not wait\\n- The Stories section has guide articles for the newest race\\n- The classics row at the bottom has the quick ones\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Play Daily free?\\nYes, with ads. The cookie popup lists 315 partners with Settings and Accept all, and a sticky banner stays at the bottom of every page. A paid plan removes the ads, and the site says every game stays free regardless.\\n\\nDoes Play Daily work on a phone?\\nYes. The page says the letter grid plays by dragging across tiles.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Play Daily?\\nNo. Every game plays without signing in, the sign-in is only for the paid ad-free plan.\\n\\nHow often do the games on Play Daily change?\\nThe daily race resets at midnight UTC per the site\'s own guide, and the unlimited and classic games can be played any time.\\n\\nDoes Play Daily save my progress?\\nPartly. A daily progress record is kept in your browser on this device.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-fake-or-fact","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/fake-or-fact/","name":"Fake or Fact","categoryId":"which-is-which","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A fast-paced trivia showdown where you separate absolute truth from total internet fiction. Can you spot the lies?","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-one-minute-detective","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/one-minute-detective/","name":"One Minute Detective","categoryId":"mystery-solve","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Channel your inner Sherlock and crack mysterious crime cases before the sixty-second timer runs out. Tik-tok, detective.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-emoji-phrase","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/emoji-phrase/","name":"Emoji Phrase","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Decode pop culture phrases, hit movies, and famous idioms written entirely in glorious emoji hieroglyphics. 🍿🎬👀","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-would-you-rather","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/would-you-rather/","name":"Would You Rather","categoryId":"tough-calls","ranking":21,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Confront impossible, hilarious dilemmas and find out just how weird your choices are compared to everyone else.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-bad-translator","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/bad-translator/","name":"Bad Translator","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":45,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Feed any normal phrase into the machine and watch it translate through multiple languages until it turns into beautiful, unhinged gibberish.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBad translator is a guessing game about machine translation gone wrong. A familiar English phrase has been passed through a chain of languages and back again, and what comes out is a mangled cousin of the original. You see the mangled version and pick the real phrase from four options. Daily mode gives you five rounds with a mix from slightly off to completely lost in translation, and practice mode keeps dealing phrases until you miss.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nChoose daily or practice and press start. Read the broken sentence, ideally out loud, and decide which of the four originals it came from, because the rhythm often survives when the words do not. After you answer, the game shows the chain of languages the phrase traveled through, so you can see where the damage happened. Daily mode scores you out of five. Practice is endless, random, and stops at your first miss.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe comedy is machine-made, not written: the phrases are pre-generated translation chains, and the results have the specific wrongness that only a machine produces, the grammar bent and the meaning gone. Seeing the language chain afterward is the best part, because you start to learn which hops do the most harm. Common sayings and film quotes turn up a lot, which makes the good guesses feel earned.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nEveryone has laughed at a bad translation, and we built it because that laugh deserved to be a game. It tests your ear for idiom rather than your memory for facts, since the rhythm of a saying often survives when the words do not. Daily mode is five rounds and done, practice runs until you miss, and either way you leave knowing which language hops do the most damage.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Read the mangled text aloud, broken grammar often hides a familiar saying\\n- Look at the language chain after each answer and learn the pattern\\n- Daily first, then practice to sharpen up\\n- Film quotes and proverbs come up often, keep them in mind\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Bad translator free?\\nYes. It is one of our own arcade games, no account and no ads.\\n\\nDoes Bad translator work on a phone?\\nYes. Tap an option on a phone or click on a computer.\\n\\nHow often does Bad translator get new phrases?\\nDaily mode has five new phrases each day. Practice mode draws from the whole pool at random.\\n\\nDoes Bad translator have a score?\\nYes. Daily mode is scored out of five. Practice keeps going until your first miss.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-odd-one-out","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/odd-one-out/","name":"Odd One Out","categoryId":"brain-train","ranking":42,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Spot the single stealthy imposter hidden inside a massive grid of identical shapes before time runs out. Your eyes will betray you.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-daily-dungeon-door","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/daily-dungeon-door/","name":"Daily Dungeon Door","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":52,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A daily game of high-stakes door-picking logic. Will you uncover legendary treasure, or are you just opening a direct gateway to your own pixelated doom?","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nDaily Dungeon Door is a push-your-luck game played on three doors, one of our own arcade games. Each day there is a new dungeon of five floors, and each floor shows three tall painted doors, purple, gold and dark red on one day, each with its name, its risk and two percentages printed under it: the chance of a trap and the chance of a rare find. One day\'s first floor offered a lost relic at medium risk, a gold hoard at high risk with a 60 percent rare chance, and a cursed pile at low risk with no trap at all.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nRead the odds, open a door. It swings aside to show what was behind it, a common broken fang and one gold, say, and a strip offers the choice: Go deeper or Walk out with what is in your bag, with a note on what the next floor\'s traps run to. A trap ends the run and you keep only your first find. Clear all five floors and the page says there is a bonus chest. Everything you carry out lands in your hoard, counted out of 50 items, on this device.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe odds are printed on the doors, so every pick is a real decision rather than a coin flip, a safe common against a risky rare, and the page says traps get more likely on every floor, which makes a full bag a reason to leave. On top of the daily run there is a weekly set: four slots that want specific finds, a rare from a gold hoard door, a rare from a cursed pile door and so on, with a countdown to Sunday night and a mythic reward for filling all four. Doors that can fill a slot carry a Set badge.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nOpening a door with a printed 18 percent chance of a trap is a one-minute thrill with real math behind it, and the hoard, the weekly set and the streak give that minute somewhere to go. It is a daily that respects the word.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Your first find is always safe, so a bold first door can pay off\\n- Doors marked Set can fill a slot in the weekly set, fill all four by Sunday for a mythic item\\n- Everyone gets the same dungeon on the same day, so compare how deep you got\\n- The note under the result tells you the next floor\'s trap range before you commit\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Daily Dungeon Door free?\\nYes. One of our own arcade games, no ads, no cookie banner and nothing to buy.\\n\\nDoes Daily Dungeon Door work on a phone?\\nYes. Three big doors on a page set up for phone screens.\\n\\nDoes Daily Dungeon Door save my hoard?\\nYes. The hoard, the weekly set and your streak are kept in your browser on this device.\\n\\nHow often does Daily Dungeon Door get a new dungeon?\\nEvery day. Five floors a day, the same for everyone, and a weekly set with a Sunday night deadline.\\n\\nDoes Daily Dungeon Door have sound?\\nNo. There is no sound toggle and the page says nothing about sound.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-mini-courtroom","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/mini-courtroom/","name":"Mini Courtroom","categoryId":"mystery-solve","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Play judge, jury, and executioner in a bite-sized court where the crimes are silly and your absolute verdicts make zero legal sense.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-click-quest","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/click-quest/","name":"Click Quest","categoryId":"decision-games","ranking":14,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An RPG for lazy adventurers. Slay monsters, upgrade your gear, and conquer dungeons using nothing but your aggressive clicking finger.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-tennis","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/tennis/","name":"Tennis","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":58,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A fast, no-nonsense physics game of virtual tennis. Play a quick match against the AI without having to put on real-world athletic shorts.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nTennis is one of our own arcade games: a teal court, a magenta paddle on the left, an orange one on the right and a small amber ball. The mode screen offers a first-to-seven match against the computer at easy, normal or hard, a daily rally, or two players on one keyboard. In the daily rally the computer never misses, everyone gets the same returns that day, and the score is how long you keep the ball alive.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick a mode, press space to serve, and move your paddle with the arrow keys, W and S, or by dragging on the play area on a phone. Every return makes the ball a touch faster. Catch it on the tip of your paddle, marked by light marks, for a power shot, faster and flatter. In two-player, the left paddle uses W and S and the right one the arrows. The computer scored on us right after the first serve.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe daily rally turns a two-minute paddle game into something you can compare. The computer returns everything and the pattern is the same for everyone that day, so your longest rally is a fair number to send to a friend, and you can try as often as you like. Beaten computer levels are ticked off on the mode screen, and the power shot adds a gamble to every return: aim too far out and the ball slips past you.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThe paddle game is the shortest route from bored to not bored, which is why we built one. A match to seven is over quickly, and the daily rally gives it a reason to come back, since the computer never misses and everyone gets the same returns that day, so your longest rally is a fair number to send to a friend. Five minutes is the brief, and it keeps to it.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Wide angles beat the easy and normal computer, they react late and drift to the middle\\n- Against hard, stay near the center and expect power shots back\\n- Power shots come off the last few pixels of the paddle, the marks show where\\n- In the daily rally a steady center hit is safer than a gamble\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Tennis free?\\nYes. It is one of our own games and costs nothing: nothing is advertised, nothing asks you to sign in, no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes Tennis work on a phone?\\nYes. Drag on the play area to move your paddle. Two-player mode needs a keyboard.\\n\\nDoes Tennis save anything?\\nYes. Beaten levels are ticked off on the mode screen and the daily rally remembers whether you played today, in your browser, as the rest of the arcade does.\\n\\nDoes Tennis end?\\nYes. A match ends at seven points. The daily rally ends when you miss, and you can go again.\\n\\nDo I need a keyboard for Tennis?\\nFor two players, yes. Alone, arrows or W and S on a desktop, drag on a phone.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-10-06","desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-brick","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/brick/","name":"Brick","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":45,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A beautifully minimalist block-breaking arcade throwback. Deflect the ball, shatter the wall, and lose track of the next twenty minutes.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBrick is a ball-and-paddle game with a daily wall, one of our own arcade games. Six rows of rounded bricks in red, orange, yellow, green, teal and blue sit in the day\'s layout on a dark navy field, an amber ball rests on a small yellow paddle, and two tabs above the play area switch between Daily wall and Classic. The daily card names the day\'s layout, a heavy diamond of 36 bricks on one day, and shows three medal times, with par in the header.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nOn the daily wall, press Start the clock, then launch. The clock starts at your first launch and stops when the last brick breaks. Move the paddle with the arrow keys, A and D, or drag on a phone. Bricks with a dark frame take two hits, an M brick drops a tile that splits the ball in three, a W brick drops a wider paddle. A lost ball never ends the run, it adds three seconds and a fresh ball appears on the paddle, with a caption telling you the clock is still running. The page says a faint ghost of the autopilot that set par plays alongside you and clears the wall right at par, so the job is to finish before it. Your first three runs of the day count for a medal: gold for five seconds under par, silver at par, bronze within ten. After that you can keep practicing. Classic is the original: a full rainbow in pyramid, diamond, zigzag, heart and arrow layouts, falling letter tiles marked 3, W, L and S that split the ball, widen the paddle, add a life or slow the action, and three lives.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nRacing a ghost instead of a score changes the feel. You can see the autopilot working through the same wall a brick at a time, and the page says lost-ball seconds land on your clock, not the ghost\'s, so a dropped ball means beating it by three. The first two balls of the day show a faint aim line, and threading the ball up through a one-brick gap counts as a trick shot, just for show. Everyone gets the same wall, so par and medal times mean the same thing to everyone.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nBreaking bricks has never stopped being fun, and a timed daily wall with a visible ghost gives it a reason to come back tomorrow. Three medal runs is the right size for a coffee break.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Aim with the edge of the paddle, the angle decides where the ball goes\\n- Go for the M brick early, three balls clear a wall much faster than one\\n- Near par, a safe return beats a risky angle, a lost ball is three seconds\\n- Your first run already counts for a medal, so treat it like the real thing\\n- Break a tunnel through one column, the page\'s last tip\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Brick free?\\nYes. One of our own arcade games, no ads, no cookie banner and nothing to buy.\\n\\nDoes Brick work on a phone?\\nYes. The page says you drag to move the paddle.\\n\\nDoes Brick save my progress?\\nYes. Your medal runs for the day are kept in your browser on this device.\\n\\nHow often does Brick get a new wall?\\nEvery day. The daily wall is a fresh layout each day, the same for everyone, and classic mode is always there.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Brick?\\nNo. Press Start the clock.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-bumpy","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/bumpy/","name":"Bumpy","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":41,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Flap the sleepy Bored.com face through red hot columns, gobble cookies that make it bigger and reach bed at the end of today\'s daily course.","dateAdded":"2026-05-20","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nBumpy is a one-button flying game and one of our own arcade games. The hero is the sleepy face from the Bored.com logo, which dozes in mid air until your first flap. From there you steer it through the gaps between yellow columns whose ends glow red hot. Every gap holds a cookie, and each one is a point and makes Bumpy a little bigger, so the game gets harder because you are doing well.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick Daily course or Endless on the start card and press Start. Tap, click or press the space bar to flap. Each flap pushes Bumpy up and gravity pulls it back down. Get through a gap and its cookie flies into Bumpy\'s mouth without any aiming from you. Hit a column or the ground and the run is over. The daily course is the same for everyone that day: 30 gaps on the way to Bumpy\'s bed, three tries, and your best try counts. Between some pairs of columns a golden cookie floats above or below both gaps. It does not come to you, so you have to dive or climb for it, and it is worth 3 points. Endless has no finish line, a new layout every run and a best score kept on your device.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe cookies are the difficulty curve. Bumpy starts small and easy to steer, then grows with every gap until it barely fits. From your second daily try a faint gray Bumpy replays your previous try, so you can see exactly where it went wrong. The result card counts the gaps you got through, the golden cookies you took and your best of the day.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThree tries a day on the daily course is a sensible ration: enough to learn the course, not enough to lose the afternoon. Everyone gets the same gaps and the same golden cookies, so comparing with a friend is fair, and the gold adds a second question to a good run, which is whether you were greedy enough.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Short, light flaps work better than mashing the button\\n- Aim for the center of the gap, Bumpy falls fast once you stop flapping\\n- Use the first cookies to find a rhythm while Bumpy is still small\\n- Go for a golden cookie right after a gap, so you have time to line up for the next column\\n- On a phone, tap anywhere on the sky, you do not need to hit Bumpy\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Bumpy free?\\nYes. It is one of our own arcade games, with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes Bumpy work on a phone?\\nYes. Tap anywhere on the sky to flap, or use the space bar on a computer.\\n\\nHow often does the daily course in Bumpy change?\\nEvery day at midnight UTC. You get three tries and your best score counts.\\n\\nDoes Bumpy save my best score?\\nYes. Your endless best and today\'s daily result are kept in your browser on the device you play on.\\n\\nDoes Bumpy end?\\nThe daily course does, after 30 gaps. Endless goes on until you hit something.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-25"},{"id":"tasteatlas-com","url":"https://www.tasteatlas.com/","name":"TasteAtlas","categoryId":"geo-explore","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An interactive global map of local food, traditional dishes, and regional ingredients. Travel the world one bite at a time without ever chewing.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"futureme-org","url":"https://www.futureme.org/","name":"FutureMe","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":27,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Write a letter to your future self and receive it years down the road. A slow-burn existential rabbit hole.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nFutureMe is a form that emails you a letter from yourself years from now. The home page is a letter box that starts with Dear FutureMe, a delivery picker and an email field. The site says it has sent over 20 million letters in 20 years and has been doing this since 2002. There is a blog on goal setting, mindfulness and how to write the letter, and a public letters section where other people\'s anonymous letters can be read.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nWrite the letter. Pick a delivery: six months, one, three, five or ten years, or a date of your own. Choose Private or Public but anonymous. Enter your email and press Send to the Future. The page says a confirmation email follows and asks you to make sure the address is correct, since the whole point arrives there. An Inspire me button opens a list of prompts: your next birthday, a story in present tense about your life in five years, a letter to yourself at your parents\' age. A Full screen toggle sits on the letter box. The page says writing a letter signs you up, and that an account is only needed to write to someone other than yourself.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe payoff is deliberately out of reach. Nothing happens today beyond a confirmation, and the thing you made turns up when you have forgotten it, which is the entire design. The public letters add a second use: reading a stranger\'s letter to themselves, with the written date, the delivery date and the time traveled shown on the card, and the page says you sometimes find out what happened next.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nWriting to a person who does not exist yet is a good way to spend ten minutes being honest, and the site has been doing the slow half of the job for a long time, by its own account. The ten-year option is the one to pick if you want a real shock later.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Check the email address twice, it is the only delivery route\\n- The Inspire me button lists prompts if the blank page stalls you\\n- The Full screen toggle on the letter box gives you more room to write\\n- Public but anonymous puts the letter in the reading section for others\\n- Six months is the shortest preset, ten years the longest\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs FutureMe free?\\nYes, with ads and a heavy cookie popup. The popup lists 210 partners with Consent or Manage options, and the options panel has all purposes off with a Confirm choices button. The page has nine ad slots.\\n\\nDoes FutureMe work on a phone?\\nYes. The form fits a phone screen.\\n\\nDo I need an account for FutureMe?\\nNot for a letter to yourself. The email address is the account in practice, and the page says a full sign-up is only needed to write to someone else.\\n\\nDoes FutureMe save my letter?\\nOn the site, not in your browser. The letter is stored by the service and emailed to you on the date you chose.\\n\\nDoes FutureMe have sound?\\nNo. It is a text form.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"10fastfingers-com","url":"https://10fastfingers.com/","name":"10FastFingers","categoryId":"typing-speed","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The legendary, high-speed keyboard test where your words-per-minute count is the only metric that defines your corporate worth.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"dwitter-net","url":"https://www.dwitter.net/","name":"Dwitter","categoryId":"coding-play","ranking":2,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A creative sandbox where programmers make visual art animations in exactly 140 characters of JavaScript. What they squeeze out of one line is absurd.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"music-map-com","url":"https://www.music-map.com/","name":"Music-Map","categoryId":"sound-discovery","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Type in any band or musical artist and watch a floating typographic nebula form to map out related music tastes.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"literature-map-com","url":"https://www.literature-map.com/","name":"Literature-Map","categoryId":"odd-search","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The tourist guide to the world of literature. Type your favorite author to generate an explorable star cluster of similar writers.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"earthcam-com","url":"https://www.earthcam.com/","name":"EarthCam Live Cams","categoryId":"geo-explore","ranking":20,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Travel the world in real time through a massive global network of live webcams capturing streets, beaches, and landmarks.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"heavens-above-com","url":"https://www.heavens-above.com/","name":"Heavens-Above Satellite Tracker","categoryId":"space-cosmos","ranking":8,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Get hyper-accurate pass times for the International Space Station and real-time tracking maps for orbiting satellites customized to your coordinates.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"superbad-com","url":"https://www.superbad.com/","name":"Superbad Web Art Installation","categoryId":"old-net-art","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A legendary, Webby-winning 1997 digital art project that leads you down a highly surreal maze of clicking chaos and visual loops.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"mcdle-net","url":"https://www.mcdle.net/","name":"MCdle","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":38,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Wordle meets the blocky universe. Test your game knowledge by guessing the daily Minecraft mob, item, block, or crafting recipe before you run out of attempts.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"classic-minecraft-net","url":"https://classic.minecraft.net/","name":"Minecraft Classic","categoryId":"tiny-towns","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A digital time machine back to 2009. Play the original, bare-bones Alpha release of Minecraft directly in your browser tab, complete with all its glorious, retro quirks.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nMinecraft Classic is the free browser version of an early 2009 build of the block game, version 0.0.23a_01, kept online on the game\'s own domain. It is a small world of colored blocks, a hotbar of nine block types, and nothing else. No survival mode, nothing to craft, no menus beyond a tiny one. You place blocks and you remove them, and that is the whole game.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nThe page opens straight into a world, first person, crosshair in the middle. Move with the WASD keys and look around with the mouse. Left click removes the block you are looking at, right click places the one selected in your hotbar. Escape opens a small game menu with options, a button to generate a new level, and back to game. The world is stored in your browser as you build, so closing the tab does not lose it.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nIt is a time capsule. Everything that made the game famous later is missing, and what is left is oddly calming: grass, dirt, stone and water under a cloudy sky, nine block types and no goal at all. The page shows no ads, no cookie banner and no login, which is rare for anything this well known. It is also the version with the least to learn: two mouse buttons and four keys.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nHardly anybody has seen this version, and everybody has heard of the game. It is the answer to what did it look like at the start, playable in the time it takes to ask. It needs nothing installed and asks for nothing, so it opens on any computer with a browser.\\n\\nTips:\\n- The world is kept in your browser, clearing site data wipes it\\n- Generate new level from the Escape menu when you want a fresh world\\n- Select a block in the hotbar before you right click, that is the one that gets placed\\n- Do not expect the later game\'s tools, animals or crafting, the hotbar is the whole kit\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Minecraft Classic free?\\nYes. It runs in the browser with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes Minecraft Classic work on a phone?\\nNot well. It expects a keyboard and mouse, so a laptop or desktop is the place to play it.\\n\\nDoes Minecraft Classic save anything?\\nYes. The world is stored in your browser automatically, so it is gone if you clear site data.\\n\\nDoes Minecraft Classic end?\\nNo. There is no goal and nothing to finish. You build until you stop.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-26","desktopOnly":true,"daily":false},{"id":"pixelpapercraft-com","url":"https://www.pixelpapercraft.com/","name":"Pixel Papercraft","categoryId":"niche-obsessions","ranking":15,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Pull your digital creations into the real world. Access a massive, user-submitted warehouse of printable papercraft templates to fold your own physical blocks and mobs.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"minecraft-novaskin-me","url":"https://minecraft.novaskin.me/","name":"Nova Skin","categoryId":"blank-canvas","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Paint your digital avatar layer by layer. An interactive 3D skin editor and scene generator that lets you design custom costumes and render characters into stylized wallpapers.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-void-skirmish","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/void-skirmish/","name":"Void Skirmish","categoryId":"action-games","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Dodge blinding bullet patterns and blast through waves of hostile space fleets in this hyper-addictive, twin-stick cosmic shooter. Don\'t blink, or the sector boss will turn your ship into stardust.","dateAdded":"2026-05-21","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"poki-com-en-stickman","url":"https://poki.com/en/stickman","name":"Stickman Games on Poki","categoryId":"stickman-games","ranking":17,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A deep repository of stick-figure chaos. Relive the glory days of school computer labs where lines beat lines to a pixelated pulp.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"mentalfloss-com","url":"https://www.mentalfloss.com/","name":"Mental Floss","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":23,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The holy grail of weird trivia and obscure facts. Excellent for becoming the most fascinatingly annoying person at any party.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"poki-com-en-g-two-button-bounce","url":"https://poki.com/en/g/two-button-bounce","name":"Two Button Bounce","categoryId":"co-op-games","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A physics platformer with a control scheme so simple it will make you and your co-op partner question your collective motor skills.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"odditycentral-com","url":"https://www.odditycentral.com","name":"Oddity Central","categoryId":"offbeat-news","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A fascinating showcase of the world\'s strangest news, oddest subcultures, and most bizarre human achievements.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"upi-com-odd-news","url":"https://www.upi.com/Odd_News/","name":"UPI Odd News","categoryId":"offbeat-news","ranking":1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Real, unhinged, and completely true weird news stories from around the globe, straight from United Press International.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"oddee-com","url":"https://www.oddee.com","name":"Oddee","categoryId":"offbeat-news","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A directory of the world\'s oddities, featuring bite-sized lists of everything strange, bizarre, and completely unexpected.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"apnews-com-oddities","url":"https://apnews.com/oddities","name":"AP News Oddities","categoryId":"offbeat-news","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The Associated Press\'s official repository for the world\'s most baffling headlines and offbeat news occurrences.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"news-sky-com-offbeat","url":"https://news.sky.com/offbeat","name":"Sky News Offbeat","categoryId":"offbeat-news","ranking":2,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Bizarre international stories, strange animal antics, and completely offbeat news from the Sky News desk.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"damninteresting-com","url":"https://www.damninteresting.com","name":"Damn Interesting","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":52,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Intricate, well-researched true stories from history and science that will completely steal your afternoon.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"livescience-com","url":"https://www.livescience.com","name":"Live Science","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":15,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Everything from ancient archaeological mysteries to the weirdest behaviors of the natural world, in one busy science hub.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"discovermagazine-com","url":"https://www.discovermagazine.com","name":"Discover Magazine","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A mix of mind-bending science news, quirky trivia, and deep dives into how psychology, physics, and the natural world actually work.","dateAdded":"2026-05-22","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"tixy-land","url":"https://tixy.land/","name":"Tixy.land","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Animate a 16x16 grid of dots using a single line of creative JavaScript code. Deceptively simple, impossibly addictive.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"dinahmoelabs-com-plink","url":"https://dinahmoelabs.com/plink/","name":"Plink","categoryId":"music-makers","ranking":21,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Hop into a real-time multiplayer grid workspace where clicking and trailing with total strangers yields surprisingly clean collaborative electronic jams.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"david-li","url":"https://david.li/","name":"David.li Web Toys","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":35,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A spectacular static catalog of fluid engines and physics sandbox systems that bend natural law right inside your active browser viewport.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nDavid.li Web Toys is a portfolio page: a white grid of twelve picture tiles, each a rendered still of something squishy, swirling or googly-eyed, with a caption under it and one line at the bottom about making interactive playthings with math, sound, code and squishiness. Six tiles open toys on the site itself: Fluid Paint, Fluid Particles, Vortex Spheres, Volumetric Particle Flow, Fourier Image Filtering and Ocean Wave Simulation. The other six go elsewhere, three to a large company\'s online arts platform and three to a TV network\'s site.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick a tile. Take Fluid Particles: a wireframe box where you first draw blocks of fluid on the walls, with a particle density slider at 30720, then press start and the blocks become a slab of blue beads that slumps and sloshes under gravity in real time. Drag rotates the camera, scroll zooms, moving the mouse pushes the particles, and sliders for fluidity and speed are there to change how it pours. Edit takes you back to the box.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nFluid Particles is a real-time physics simulation running in a browser tab, presented as a toy rather than a demo, and the captions suggest its neighbors are the same. There is no walkthrough and no score, just a few control hints, a box of water and your cursor. The hub is the right link because it lets you pick: paint that flows, spheres in a vortex, an ocean surface, a Fourier image filter.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nPlenty of pages let a cursor leave a pretty trail. Here the cursor pushes actual simulated water, a slab of blue beads that slumps and sloshes in real time, and the neighboring tiles promise more of the same. Nothing to learn, everything to poke, and no score to chase. It is the page you open to show someone what a browser can do now, best on a desktop with a mouse.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with Fluid Particles, draw one big block and press start\\n- Turn speed down to watch the slosh in slow motion\\n- Scroll in close, the individual beads are the show\\n- Three tiles link out to a TV network over plain http, so they may not open everywhere\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs David.li Web Toys free?\\nYes. No ad, no shop, no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes David.li Web Toys work on a phone?\\nPartly. The pages have no phone layout and Fluid Particles leans on scroll, drag and shift-drag, so a desktop with a mouse is the way to see them.\\n\\nDoes David.li Web Toys save anything?\\nNo. Fluid Particles starts fresh on every load.\\n\\nDoes David.li Web Toys have sound?\\nNot on the hub or in Fluid Particles. The self-description mentions sound, so some tiles may have it.\\n\\nDoes David.li Web Toys end?\\nNo. Each toy runs until you close it.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-10-06","desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"paperplanes-world","url":"https://paperplanes.world/","name":"Paper Planes World","categoryId":"crowd-experiments","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Fold a digital paper plane, stamp it with your location, and cast it out into a global network to be caught and stamped by strangers across the earth.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"openprocessing-org","url":"https://openprocessing.org/","name":"OpenProcessing","categoryId":"coding-play","ranking":8,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Plunge into a massive community warehouse of generative artwork, open-source geometric loops, and interactive script experiments.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"mandel-gart-nz","url":"https://mandel.gart.nz/","name":"Mandelbrot Set Explorer","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A sleek, reactive fractal viewer equipped with smooth infinite zoom steps, custom color mapping, and rapid Julia set generation.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"scratch-mit-edu","url":"https://scratch.mit.edu/","name":"Scratch","categoryId":"coding-play","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Create your own games and animations using visual, snap-together blocks. A deadline-free sandbox where programming meets pure play.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"slowroads-io","url":"https://slowroads.io/","name":"Slow Roads","categoryId":"brain-reset","ranking":31,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An endless, procedurally generated driving simulator built directly in your browser. Throw on some music, tweak the weather, and just cruise forever.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"lofi-cafe","url":"https://lofi.cafe/","name":"Lofi Cafe","categoryId":"radio-streams","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A beautifully built portal streaming live lo-fi beats into cozy virtual rooms. The right backdrop for studying, working, or completely zoning out.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"tree-fm","url":"https://www.tree.fm/","name":"Tree.fm","categoryId":"brain-reset","ranking":34,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Instantly escape into the vivid, real-life audio recordings of serene forests from around the world. Perfect for masking office chaos and pretending you\'re forest bathing at your desk.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"goodnewsnetwork-org","url":"https://www.goodnewsnetwork.org/","name":"Good News Network","categoryId":"feel-good","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The definitive online antidote to the typical global doomscroll. A massive archive of exclusively positive, uplifting headlines.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"msoutlookit-vercel-app","url":"https://msoutlookit.vercel.app/","name":"MSOutlookit","categoryId":"look-productive","ranking":2,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Disguise your relentless Reddit scrolling as an urgent corporate assignment. This brilliant interface dresses the front page of the internet up as a fake Microsoft Outlook inbox.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"decisionproblem-com-paperclips","url":"https://www.decisionproblem.com/paperclips/","name":"Universal Paperclips","categoryId":"idle-clicker-games","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A masterfully deceptive incremental clicker game where you play an AI tasked with manufacturing paperclips. What begins with a single click quickly expands into total cosmic dominance.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"fakeupdate-net","url":"https://fakeupdate.net/","name":"Fake Update","categoryId":"prank-screens","ranking":44,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Trigger a highly convincing, never-ending full-screen operating system update on your monitor. The absolute ultimate excuse to walk away from your desk and avoid real work.","dateAdded":"2026-05-24","affiliate":false,"desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-tube-dash","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/tube-dash/","name":"Tube Dash","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Navigate a high-speed neon tunnel and dodge moving obstacles before your ship gets turned into scrap metal. Fast, hypnotic, and wildly addictive.","dateAdded":"2026-05-26","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nTube Dash is one of our own arcade games, an endless three-lane runner with a chunky, low-resolution 3D look. A small figure in a dark red top sprints away from the camera down a dark road with yellow lane markings, inside a sand-colored tunnel under a pale blue sky. The first stage introduces itself with a banner: Stage 1, Sunny tube.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress Start running. The runner moves forward on their own and the speed climbs over time. The left and right arrows, or A and D, switch lanes. The up arrow or the space bar jumps, and the down arrow or S slides. On a phone, swipe sideways to change lanes, up to jump and down to slide, and a tap counts as a quick jump. The page lists four kinds of obstacle: low walls to jump, overhead bars to slide under, pillars that block a whole lane, and carriages that drift sideways into your lane as you approach. One hit and the run ends. A distance readout sits in the top right corner and boxes for score and coins in the bottom left.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nCoins lie in the lane ahead, and pickups turn up among them. The page says a magnet pulls nearby coins toward you for six seconds, a jet pack flies you over everything for five seconds while collecting coins, and a score multiplier doubles every point for six seconds. The start card says there are five stages and that the speed and intensity climb the further you go.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThree lanes, two moves and one rule about not hitting things is most of what a runner needs. The magnets and jet packs are a bonus, and New run is one button away.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Commit to a lane early, the page warns that a half-finished switch still counts as a hit\\n- A slide cancels a jump and a jump cancels a slide, so inputs can be chained\\n- Carriages start outside your lane and drift in as you get close\\n- Pillars never move, so change lanes well ahead of them\\n- On a phone, swipe inside the game area, swipes outside it do not register\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Tube Dash free?\\nYes. No ads, no cookie banner, no account.\\n\\nDoes Tube Dash work on a phone?\\nYes. Swipe to change lanes, jump and slide, or tap for a quick jump.\\n\\nDoes Tube Dash end?\\nNot on its own. It is an endless runner, and a run lasts until the first hit.\\n\\nDoes Tube Dash save my score?\\nYes. The page says your best score and best distance are saved on your device.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-24"},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-crypt-rush","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/crypt-rush/","name":"Crypt Rush","categoryId":"fps-games","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Dash through trap-filled pixelated catacombs to hoard ancient gold before the floors drop or the shadows catch you. Pure old-school arcade anxiety.","dateAdded":"2026-05-26","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-acorn-rain","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/acorn-rain/","name":"Acorn Rain","categoryId":"defense-games","ranking":1,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Stockpile falling nuts while navigating structural chaos in this lighthearted physics puzzle. Simple mechanics, but entirely impossible to play just once.","dateAdded":"2026-05-26","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"thewikigame-com","url":"https://thewikigame.com/","name":"The Wiki Game","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":5,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Race against the clock from one random Wikipedia page to another using only blue hyperlinks. Deep-wiki speed-running at its finest.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"ptable-com","url":"https://ptable.com/","name":"Dynamic Periodic Table (Ptable)","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":24,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"An interactive periodic table with every bell and whistle. Toggle through orbitals, test isotopes, or watch states of matter change with a temperature slider. Chemistry has never been this clickable.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"geo-fs-com","url":"https://www.geo-fs.com/","name":"GeoFS","categoryId":"sims-sandboxes","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Take to the skies in a free browser flight simulator built on real global satellite maps. Cruise anywhere in the world from your browser cockpit.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"actorle-com","url":"https://actorle.com/","name":"Actorle","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":37,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A daily guessing game for cinephiles. Deduce the mystery actor using their chronological filmography, genre tags, and movie ratings.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"cantunsee-space","url":"https://cantunsee.space/","name":"Can\'t Unsee","categoryId":"design-games","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A deceptively simple game that challenges your design eye to spot microscopic layout differences. Your attention to detail is about to be humiliated.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"typatone-com","url":"https://typatone.com/","name":"Typatone","categoryId":"music-makers","ranking":19,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Turn your mundane keyboard typing into an impossibly beautiful, relaxing ambient melody. Suddenly your emails sound like a classical masterpiece.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"gridland-doublespeakgames-com","url":"https://gridland.doublespeakgames.com/","name":"Gridland","categoryId":"strategy-games","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A brilliant match-3 survival game where you build structures by day and match weapons to fight monsters by night. Deceptively strategic and utterly addictive.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"madebyevan-com-webgl-water","url":"https://madebyevan.com/webgl-water/","name":"WebGL Water Simulator","categoryId":"sims-sandboxes","ranking":23,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Interact with a photorealistic, beautifully fluid digital pool. Toss a ball in, trigger ripples, and marvel at what a browser rendering engine can do when it flexes.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"politicalcompass-org","url":"https://www.politicalcompass.org/","name":"The Political Compass","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Take a quick multi-axis quiz to map out your core socio-political ideology. Find out exactly which historical figures you\'d agree with (or argue with) at a dinner party.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"diep-io","url":"https://diep.io/","name":"Diep.io","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":20,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Upgrade your geometric tank, destroy obstacles, and survive an arena packed with hostile players. Tactical multiplayer chaos that hits all the right dopamine triggers.","dateAdded":"2026-05-28","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"worldle-teuteuf-fr","url":"https://worldle.teuteuf.fr/","name":"Worldle","categoryId":"geo-games","ranking":19,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Wordle, but make it geographic. Guess the daily mystery country based entirely on its silhouette and distance vector clues.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"travle-earth","url":"https://travle.earth/","name":"Travle","categoryId":"geo-games","ranking":14,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Travel from point A to point B by naming the fewest bordering nations. A brilliant way to realize you don\'t know geography as well as you think you do.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikitrivia-tomjwatson-com","url":"https://wikitrivia.tomjwatson.com/","name":"WikiTrivia","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":35,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Drag and drop historical events, inventions, and historical figures onto an open timeline. One chronological error and your digital streak is history.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"higherlowergame-com","url":"https://www.higherlowergame.com/","name":"The Higher Lower Game","categoryId":"estimation-games","ranking":17,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Does a global financial crisis get searched more than global warming? Test your cultural intuition against real-world Google search numbers.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nThe Higher Lower Game is a quiz with one question repeated forever: which of these two things do more people search for? A band on the left with its monthly search count showing, a plane maker on the right with its count hidden, and two buttons, higher or lower. Get it right and the right-hand card slides over to become the next comparison. Get it wrong and the run ends. That loop is the whole game.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick classic mode to start. Read the left card, guess whether the right one is searched for more or less often, press the button, and watch the real number roll in. Your score is your streak, and the page keeps your high score on screen. Beat the clock mode adds a timer, and there is a newer elimination mode the site is still testing. The pairs mix the obvious with the genuinely unguessable, which is where most runs die.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nIt is less a trivia game than a test of your model of other people. You do not need to know anything, you need to know what the world is curious about, and the world is curious about odd things. The site is upfront that its numbers come from a snapshot taken in 2017, so treat it as a period piece about what the internet cared about that year.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nOne guess, one reveal, and a streak that ends the moment your instinct is off. The game asks you to put a number on something you could never know exactly, how many people search for a thing, and the pairs are built so your sense of scale fails in interesting places. It takes under a minute to explain and is dangerously replayable, since every run ends with a number you should have seen coming.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Think about how many people would type it, not how important it is\\n- Everyday things get searched for far more than fame suggests, keep that in mind\\n- Try beat the clock once you have a feel for the scale\\n- The numbers are from 2017, so recent fame does not count\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs The Higher Lower Game free?\\nYes. It is free in the browser with no account. There is a cookie notice on the first visit.\\n\\nDoes The Higher Lower Game work on a phone?\\nYes. It works in a mobile browser, and there is also an app on Google Play.\\n\\nDoes The Higher Lower Game end?\\nEach run ends at your first wrong answer, and your high score stays on the page so you can chase it.\\n\\nAre the numbers in The Higher Lower Game current?\\nNo. The site says the search counts are global monthly figures from 2017.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"narrow-one","url":"https://narrow.one/","name":"Narrow One","categoryId":"io-games","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Grab your bow, rally your teammates, and defend the castle walls in this beautifully fluid, multiplayer 3D archery arena.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"ocearch-org-tracker","url":"https://www.ocearch.org/tracker/","name":"OCEARCH Shark Tracker","categoryId":"nature-watch","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A real-time satellite tracking map mapping tagged sharks, whales, and sea turtles swimming through global marine waters.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"procatinator-com","url":"https://procatinator.com/","name":"Procatinator","categoryId":"just-cats","ranking":2,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A time capsule matching random cat animations with legendary synth melodies. Peak digital procrastination fuel.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"dogeminer2-com","url":"https://dogeminer2.com/","name":"Doge Miner 2","categoryId":"idle-clicker-games","ranking":16,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Tap your way to lunar dominance, hire helpful shiba workers, and accumulate massive dogecoin fortunes in this meme-stuffed idle clicker game.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"adarkroom-doublespeakgames-com","url":"https://adarkroom.doublespeakgames.com/","name":"A Dark Room","categoryId":"text-games","ranking":18,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A cold room. A fading fire. What starts as a simple text prompt slowly unravels into a massive, intensely atmospheric web-based survival adventure.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"idrlabs-com","url":"https://www.idrlabs.com/tests.php","name":"IDRlabs","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Dive down a massive wormhole of psychological, political, and cultural alignment charts to discover who you really are (or which fictional villain you resemble).","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"googlefeud-com","url":"https://www.googlefeud.com/","name":"Google Feud","categoryId":"trivia-quiz","ranking":40,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Test your predictive instincts against the untamed chaos of the human subconscious by guessing how Google autocompletes popular search terms.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nGoogle Feud is a family-quiz show where the survey is the search engine\'s autocomplete. The page shows the start of a search, something like why does my, and your job is to guess how the world\'s most typed-in box would finish it. Ten real suggestions are hidden on the board, and the round is over once your guesses run out. It has been called an obsession by a major magazine, and the page happily quotes it.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPick a category: culture, entertainment, names, questions, animals, people or food, or let the lucky button choose. Read the half-finished search, type a guess, press enter. Hits flip open on the board with their points, misses cost you one of your strikes. Easy mode softens things, and there is a daily question of the day plus a separate daily mode in the menu.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe answers are not written by a quiz writer, they are what millions of strangers actually type, which makes every board a small survey of human worry, greed and curiosity. Guessing well means thinking like the internet, not knowing facts, and the gap between the two is where the laughs come from. The site is careful to call itself a parody and is not connected to the search engine it borrows from.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nMost quiz games test what you know. This one tests a rarer kind of knowledge, what everyone else is thinking, because the answers are whatever millions of strangers actually typed into the search box. A round is over when your strikes run out and leaves you slightly better at reading the internet\'s mind, and it plays well alone and better in a group shouting guesses at one screen.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Guess the boring, common answer first, it is usually on the board\\n- Try a few categories, some suit your brain better than others\\n- Try easy mode before the daily question\\n- Sign-in is optional, you can play without it\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Google Feud free?\\nYes. It is free to play in the browser without an account. The page is ad supported and shows a cookie popup on the first visit.\\n\\nDoes Google Feud work on a phone?\\nYes. Typing guesses works fine on a phone keyboard.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Google Feud?\\nNo. There is an optional sign-in, but the game plays without it.\\n\\nDoes Google Feud end?\\nEach round ends when your wrong guesses run out, and the guess counter is on screen. The daily modes give one puzzle a day, the categories are endless.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-25","daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"98-js-org","url":"https://98.js.org/","name":"Windows 98 in JavaScript","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":29,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Travel back to 1998 with this fully operational browser-based replica of Windows 98, complete with Paint, Minesweeper, and classic system errors.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"neal-fun-cursor-camp","url":"https://neal.fun/cursor-camp/","name":"Cursor Camp","categoryId":"crowd-experiments","ranking":11,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Gather around a virtual campfire with hundreds of other live cursors. It\'s a cozy crowd experiment where every movement builds a collective digital canvas.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"animagraffs-com","url":"https://animagraffs.com/","name":"Animagraffs","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Ever wondered how a jet engine or a tattoo machine actually works? Take apart complex mechanics with gorgeous interactive 3D animated infographics.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"blobmixer-14islands-com","url":"https://blobmixer.14islands.com/","name":"Blobmixer","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":17,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Create, customize, and mash highly reflective, rubbery 3D blobs. It\'s a gorgeous digital sandbox of satisfying physics and color variations.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":true},{"id":"parseword-com","url":"https://www.parseword.com/","name":"Parseword","categoryId":"word-nerd","ranking":12,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A clean, minimalist daily word game that tests your analytical vocabulary muscle before your morning caffeine kicks in.","dateAdded":"2026-05-29","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"dinosaur-game-io","url":"https://dinosaur-game.io","name":"Dinosaur Game","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"The legendary pixelated T-Rex endless runner. Tap space to hop over desert cacti, duck under pesky pterodactyls, and chase your high score.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nDinosaur Game is a fan remake of the pixel dinosaur runner from a browser\'s offline error page. This version runs online and adds a leaderboard. The game sits at the top of a white page: a thin ground line, a small green dinosaur on the left and a five-digit counter in the top right corner.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress the space bar and the dinosaur starts running. The ground scrolls, the counter climbs and cacti come in from the right. The page lists two controls: space or the up arrow jumps over obstacles, and the down arrow ducks under low-flying pterodactyls. The job, in the page\'s words, is jumping over obstacles, avoiding collisions and running as far as possible. A row of small buttons above the game shows your guest name, your best score, a difficulty picker with Easy, Normal and Hard, a leaderboard link and a zoom setting.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe original was something you met by accident when the connection dropped. This one is a place you go on purpose, so it comes with things the accident never had: three difficulty levels, a guest name handed out on arrival, and boards for all time, today, this week and this month, split by difficulty. There is also a Most Played table. Below the game the page carries long articles about the runner\'s history, for anyone who wants the backstory of a dinosaur and some cacti.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nThe original only turned up when the connection dropped, which made it a game nobody chose to play. Having it one click away, with the connection working, removes the only excuse for a low score.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Space and the up arrow both jump, pick one and stick with it\\n- The down arrow is for the flying ones\\n- Switch the picker above the game to Easy while you find the rhythm\\n- Your best score shows in the row above the game\\n- The fullscreen button is under the game\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Dinosaur Game free?\\nYes, and no account is needed. A cookie popup appears at the bottom on arrival. \\"More Options\\" leads to a single switch that is off by default, then \\"Save & Exit\\". The site may show ads.\\n\\nDoes Dinosaur Game work on a phone?\\nThe controls on the page are keys: space, the up arrow and the down arrow.\\n\\nDoes Dinosaur Game save my score?\\nYes. Your best score is kept in your browser.\\n\\nDoes Dinosaur Game end?\\nNot on its own. It is an endless runner, and the counter keeps climbing for as long as you keep clearing obstacles.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-24"},{"id":"sprunki-org-online","url":"https://sprunki.org/online","name":"Sprunki Online","categoryId":"music-makers","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Drag, drop, and organize quirky animated vocalists onto a virtual stage to sculpt layered, synchronized electronic beats.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nSprunki Online is a fan-made mod of the drag-and-drop music mixer with the singing characters: a row of figures on a stage, a tray of sound icons underneath, and a beat that builds as you dress each figure in a sound. This version has its own cast of gray figures and its own loops, and it plays free in the browser with nothing to install.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nPress Play and wait for the loader. Seven gray figures stand on a green hill. Below them are twenty icons in two rows: beats, effects, melodies and voices. Drag an icon onto a figure and it turns into a character and starts its loop. Add more until the track fills out. Under each active character are mute, solo and remove controls, and a reset button clears the stage. The loops play in sync, so you are building one track, not seven.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe mod scene around this mixer is enormous and this site gathers it: the front page is a directory of other mods, sorted into categories that run from casual to horror, and the player here is the standard one. The sounds are catchy in a way that surprises people who came for a joke. There is also a gallery button in the menu, best left alone on a first visit.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nIt is a toy rather than a game: no score, no goal, just a beat you made and can reset in one click. For everyone who saw a clip and wanted to try it, this is a working version, free, in a tab, with sound as the whole point.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with one beat and one melody, then add voices\\n- Use solo to hear what one character is doing before you keep it\\n- Full screen makes the drag targets bigger\\n- Headphones, this is a music toy and laptop speakers do not do it justice\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Sprunki Online free?\\nYes. It is free in the browser with no account, and no ads show around the game.\\n\\nDoes Sprunki Online work on a phone?\\nYes. Drag and drop works with touch, though a bigger screen makes the icons easier to hit.\\n\\nDoes Sprunki Online have sound?\\nYes, and it is the entire point. Play with sound on.\\n\\nDoes Sprunki Online end?\\nNo. It is a mixer with no goal. Reset clears the stage and you start again.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-26","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"drawastickman-com","url":"https://drawastickman.com/","name":"Draw a Stickman","categoryId":"adventure-games","ranking":13,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Draw your own stick figure hero and watch them come to life to battle dragons, solve puzzles, and save the day in a custom cartoon world.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":true},{"id":"lizardpoint-com","url":"https://lizardpoint.com/","name":"Lizard Point Quizzes","categoryId":"geo-games","ranking":9,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Put your geographic awareness to the test with crisp, interactive map quizzes that challenge you to find obscure global coordinates.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"29a-ch-sandbox-2011-neonflames","url":"https://29a.ch/sandbox/2011/neonflames/#","name":"Neon Flames","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":25,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Paint glowing interstellar nebulas across an infinite black vacuum with this hypnotic interactive WebGL toy.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wikipedia-org-wiki-list-of-conspiracy-theories","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_conspiracy_theories","name":"Wikipedia: List of Conspiracy Theories","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":34,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Fall down history\'s most intricate reading rabbit hole, tracking humanity\'s most bizarre alternative narratives.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"lettersofnote-com","url":"https://lettersofnote.com/","name":"Letters of Note","categoryId":"curious-facts","ranking":7,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Peer into history\'s mailboxes. Unique, humorous, and deeply moving personal letters from famous figures.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"foddy-net-athletics-html","url":"https://www.foddy.net/legacy/Athletics.html","name":"QWOP","categoryId":"pointless-fun","ranking":38,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Attempt to run a simple 100-meter dash by individually coordinating leg muscles in the world\'s most intentionally clumsy ragdoll simulator.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nQWOP is the hundred-meter sprint where you control the runner\'s legs one muscle at a time. Q and W move the thighs, O and P move the calves, and your athlete, the sole representative of a small nation whose training program was under-funded, has to get from the start line to the finish without collapsing. Most runs end in a heap a few meters in.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick to begin. The runner stands on a track with a distance readout at the top. Press Q or W to drive a thigh, O or P to drive a calf, and try to make the four of them add up to a stride. Falling over ends the run and you start again. The intro says it is not about whether you win or lose, and it means it. There is a sound toggle and a help button in the corner of the game.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nIt is a ragdoll-control joke from 2008, still on its maker\'s own site and now running in plain HTML5 with no plugin. Nothing about it has been softened: the physics are unforgiving, the runner is a puppet, and every meter is earned with a rhythm you have to work out for yourself. A few meters and a new respect for walking is the usual result, and the readout is happy to count backwards.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nA running game you cannot run in has been wasting people\'s afternoons for a long time, and it asks for nothing: no download, no account, no ads, no cookie banner. Two meters, five minutes, and you will be back.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Small taps beat held keys\\n- Watch the readout, it tells you when you went backwards\\n- Find a rhythm before you find speed\\n- Do not read tips, the point is working it out\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs QWOP free?\\nYes. It is free in the browser on its maker\'s site, with no account, no ads and no cookie banner.\\n\\nDoes QWOP work on a phone?\\nNo. It is a keyboard game, four keys, so a laptop or desktop is required.\\n\\nDoes QWOP have sound?\\nYes, small effects, with a mute button in the corner.\\n\\nDoes QWOP end?\\nYes, at 100 meters. Reaching it is the point, and very few do.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-28","desktopOnly":false,"daily":false},{"id":"flashbynight-com","url":"https://www.flashbynight.com/","name":"Flash By Night","categoryId":"arcade-portals","ranking":4,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Skip the download bars and step into a charming array of quick, browser-native logic, memory, and word mini-games.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nFlash By Night is a one-page collection of coffee-break games made by one person: forty-nine tiles on a plain grid, each a small puzzle or word game. Color-flood grids in two versions, a phonetics word game, a cipher puzzle, sliding tiles, fill-the-grid puzzles, a stacking game, rebus puzzles, mental math, word molecules, a chess variant, a flag quiz, a tune game. Despite the name, the games run in plain HTML5 with no plugin.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nClick a tile. The game opens on its own page with one line of instructions and a best score that the page keeps for you. Most take a minute to learn and five to play. There is no menu, no account and no search, because forty-nine tiles do not need one. Come back to the grid with the browser\'s back button and try the next one.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nThe scale. Where the giant portals are walls of licensed tiles, this is a single maker\'s shelf, and every game on it shares a sensibility: small, quiet, logical, a little wordy. The site has one ad banner and a small privacy notice, and nothing else between you and the grid.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nAt the other end of the scale from the giant game sites sits this one-page grid of forty-nine small puzzles. All share one sensibility, small and a little wordy. Most take a minute to learn and five to play, and the color-flood game alone is worth the click. One note: the site is served over plain http, so your browser may flag it as not secure, and there is nothing personal to type into it anyway.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Start with the color-flood puzzle, there are two versions\\n- The word games assume English, the number games do not\\n- Best scores are kept per game in your browser\\n- Do not expect fast-action games here, this is a puzzle shelf\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Flash By Night free?\\nYes. Every game is free with no account. There is one ad banner and a small privacy notice.\\n\\nDoes Flash By Night work on a phone?\\nYes. The site says play on your PC or on your phone.\\n\\nDo I need to install anything for Flash By Night?\\nNo. The games are plain HTML5 and run in any browser, whatever the name suggests.\\n\\nDoes Flash By Night save anything?\\nEach game keeps a best score in your browser. There is no account.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-09-27","daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"youarelistening-to","url":"https://youarelistening.to/","name":"You Are Listening To","categoryId":"audio-toys","ranking":6,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Drift away into a distinct ambient room combining underground electronic music with live police radio dispatch frequencies from around the globe.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"flashbynight-com-drench","url":"https://flashbynight.com/drench/","name":"Drench","categoryId":"puzzle-games","ranking":18,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Flood a matrix of pixel tiles into one single, uniform color palette before your strictly limited allocation of moves runs entirely dry.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"gotoquiz-com-pottermore-sorting-quiz-all-possible-question","url":"https://www.gotoquiz.com/pottermore_sorting_quiz_all_possible_question","name":"Full Pottermore Sorting Quiz","categoryId":"psych-tests","ranking":3,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Your true wizarding alliance, determined by an uncommonly thorough quiz that uses every known sorting question for pinpoint accuracy.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"codepen-io-akm2-full-rhisa","url":"https://codepen.io/akm2/full/rHIsa","name":"CodePen: Gravity Points","categoryId":"visual-toys","ranking":36,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Drop invisible black holes onto a interactive canvas and watch thousands of glowing particles warp and orbit in beautiful mathematical formations.","dateAdded":"2026-05-31","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"wantnostalgia-com","url":"https://wantnostalgia.com/","name":"Want Nostalgia","categoryId":"retro-web","ranking":20,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Select a decade and drown yourself in a wave of music and memories you forgot existed. Better than a literal time machine.","dateAdded":"2026-06-01","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"bored-com-arcade-katana-kitchen","url":"https://www.bored.com/arcade/katana-kitchen/","name":"Katana Kitchen","categoryId":"mini-games","ranking":10,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"Chop ingredients with a legendary samurai sword because standard chef knives are for cowards. Warning: high risk of digital food fights.","dateAdded":"2026-06-01","affiliate":false,"daily":true,"longDescription":"What it is:\\nKatana Kitchen is a slicing game with a job, one of our own arcade games. You stand behind a low-poly sushi counter looking down at a cutting board, red lanterns on the back wall, and ingredients get tossed up over the board in arcs. An order ticket hangs in the top corner, two squid, say, and slicing what the ticket asks for is the point. Three modes on the start card: Daily order, Lunch rush and Classic.\\n\\nHow to play:\\nDrag the mouse or swipe a finger across an ingredient while it is in the air. Every clean cut turns salmon, tuna, squid, avocado or sea urchin into a finished piece of sushi and counts on the Sushi tally. Fill the ticket to serve the order for a bonus, and the next ticket drops in, a little bigger each time. The daily order card says 45 seconds, the same tosses and tickets for everyone that day, with three tries. Lunch rush is a 30 second sprint you can replay as often as you like. Both count sushi, have no lives and forgive a dropped ingredient, and a full order adds three sushi. Classic is endless with points, combo multipliers and three lives, where a drop costs a life and a full order gives one back. The page says the first seconds of every run are calm, and then the wasabi bomb shows up, a lumpy green ball with a red glow: never slice it, it ruins three sushi, or costs a life and points in classic. Bombs that fall off screen are harmless.\\n\\nWhat makes it different:\\nPlenty of games let you swipe at things flying through the air. This one gives the swipe a reason: a ticket to fill while everything else is still in the air, so the clever part is restraint, cutting what the customer asked for first. The page says the daily order is the way to play, since the share line keeps the sequence secret, so a score means something next to a friend\'s.\\n\\nWhy it is on Bored:\\nTurning a raw fish into a finished piece of sushi with one swipe is the kind of small reward a thumb never tires of, and the order tickets add the one decision that keeps it from being pure reflex. Forty-five seconds a try, three tries, and a thirty second lunch rush when three tries were not enough.\\n\\nTips:\\n- Slice what the ticket asks for first, a full order is worth more than any single piece\\n- Line two or three ingredients up and cut them with one long swipe for a combo\\n- Use the calm first seconds to learn the arcs before the board gets busy\\n- Let the wasabi bomb fall, it only hurts you if your blade touches it\\n- In the daily the tosses repeat on every try, so your second try can plan ahead\\n\\nFAQ:\\nIs Katana Kitchen free?\\nYes. One of our own arcade games, no ads, no cookie banner and nothing to buy.\\n\\nDoes Katana Kitchen work on a phone?\\nYes. Swipe to slice, with a fullscreen button.\\n\\nDoes Katana Kitchen save my progress?\\nYes. The day\'s tries are kept in your browser on this device.\\n\\nHow often does Katana Kitchen get a new order?\\nEvery day. One daily order a day with the same tosses and tickets for everyone, plus lunch rush and classic any time.\\n\\nDo I need an account for Katana Kitchen?\\nNo. Pick a mode and swipe.\\n\\nReviewed: 2026-11-03","desktopOnly":false},{"id":"1000awesomethings-com","url":"https://1000awesomethings.com/","name":"1000 Awesome Things","categoryId":"feel-good","ranking":14,"multiplier":0.01,"description":"A beautiful countdown of life\'s simple, everyday pleasures. A heartwarming reminder of the tiny joys that make being alive awesome.","dateAdded":"2026-06-04","affiliate":false,"daily":false,"desktopOnly":false},{"id":"agoodmovietowatch-com","url":"https://agoodmovietowatch.com/","name":"a good movie to watch","cate